{"version":1,"locations":[{"id":"party-roller-rink","pack":"party","category":"active-venues","emoji":"🛼","name":"Roller Rink","fullName":"A Roller Skating Rink","clues":["Someone wearing neon knee pads crashes into a wall of birthday balloons.","Disco music competes with the unmistakable thud of another person falling.","Buttered popcorn mixed with rental footwear that has seen better decades."],"hint":"Somewhere you'll probably fall down","facts":[{"en":"James Plimpton patented the four-wheel quad roller skate in 1863, making turning on skates much easier."},{"en":"Roller discos became a craze in the late 1970s, mixing skating with disco music and lights."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate a pretzel that fought back.","heat":1},{"text":"I spilled nacho cheese on my knee pads.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate fries beside a wall of rented wheels.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard somebody yell, ‘I’m fine!’","heat":1},{"text":"I heard disco music and a spectacular thud.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard eight wheels rattle over the floor.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a dad pretending he wasn’t scared.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a kid glide backward past his mom.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a guard in stripes whistle at the speedsters.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a bandage for my wounded pride.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a glittery knee pad under a bench.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried boots with four wheels underneath.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my legs filed a complaint.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after my third dramatic floor hug.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when the DJ called the final lap.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was near the snack counter, mostly.","heat":1},{"text":"I was under the disco ball, rolling slowly.","heat":2},{"text":"I was in the middle of the rink, on eight wheels.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was trying not to embarrass myself.","heat":1},{"text":"I was falling down with great confidence.","heat":2},{"text":"I was skating backward. For two seconds.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-trampoline-park","pack":"party","category":"active-venues","emoji":"🤸","name":"Trampoline Park","fullName":"An Indoor Trampoline Park","clues":["A father attempts an impressive flip and lands in a mountain of colorful foam cubes.","Excited shrieks, rhythmic squeaking, and an employee repeatedly reminding everyone of the rules.","Rubber flooring, fresh socks, and warm pretzels."],"hint":"Somewhere you'll probably fall down","facts":[{"en":"The word trampoline comes from the Spanish 'trampolín', meaning diving board."},{"en":"George Nissen and Larry Griswold built an early trampoline in the 1930s, and the US Navy later used trampolines to train WWII pilots."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate a cookie that vanished in two bites.","heat":1},{"text":"I drank water like I’d crossed a desert.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate pizza while wearing sticky grip socks.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard a kid shout, ‘Watch this!’","heat":1},{"text":"I heard springs squeak beneath squealing kids.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard a foam-pit landing swallow a scream.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a grown-up lose an argument with gravity.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a kid attempt a very crooked flip.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a staffer in a red shirt patrol the bounce courts.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a sock that wasn’t mine.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a foam cube stuck to my shirt.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried neon grip socks with rubber soles.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my knees requested retirement.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after my last flip became a flop.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when my bouncing wristband expired.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was in line, waiting for my turn.","heat":1},{"text":"I was on a giant bouncy floor, mid-air.","heat":2},{"text":"I was buried up to my neck in foam cubes.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was proving I'm still young. I'm not.","heat":1},{"text":"I was doing a flip. Mostly sideways.","heat":2},{"text":"I was bouncing way too high in grip socks.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-ice-skating-rink","pack":"party","category":"active-venues","emoji":"⛸️","name":"Ice Rink","fullName":"An Ice Skating Rink","clues":["A child glides gracefully past an adult desperately gripping the railing.","Sharp scraping noises echo beneath cheerful music and occasional cries for help.","Cold air, hot chocolate, and damp winter clothing."],"hint":"Somewhere you'll probably fall down","facts":[{"en":"The oldest known ice skates were made from animal bones about 5,000 years ago."},{"en":"Frank Zamboni invented the ice resurfacing machine in 1949 in California."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I drank cocoa and burned my tongue.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate soup while my fingers thawed.","heat":2},{"text":"I drank cocoa beside a machine smoothing ice.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard someone shriek, then laugh.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard sharp blades scraping beneath the music.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard metal runners carve circles into ice.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a child cling to an exhausted dad.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a teenager glide backward in circles.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a coach demonstrate a perfect spin.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried gloves that smelled like wet pennies.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a mitten frozen against the barrier.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried boots with long metal blades.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when I couldn’t feel my toes.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after falling on the same elbow twice.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when the ice resurfacer rolled out.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was near the rental counter.","heat":1},{"text":"I was hugging the railing for dear life.","heat":2},{"text":"I was on the ice, dodging the resurfacer.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was trying to look cool. It didn't work.","heat":1},{"text":"I was sliding around on thin blades.","heat":2},{"text":"I was gliding on the ice in rented skates.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-rock-climbing-gym","pack":"party","category":"active-venues","emoji":"🧗","name":"Climbing Gym","fullName":"An Indoor Rock Climbing Gym","clues":["A teenager hangs sideways from a colorful wall while an instructor watches calmly below.","Shoes scrape against textured surfaces as someone shouts encouragement from the floor.","Chalk dust, rubber shoes, and fresh sports drinks."],"hint":"Somewhere you'll probably fall down","facts":[{"en":"One of the first artificial climbing walls was built at the University of Leeds, England, in 1964."},{"en":"Sport climbing made its Olympic debut at the Tokyo 2020 Games, held in 2021."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate a banana like it owed me money.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate a granola bar with chalky fingers.","heat":2},{"text":"I drank water beneath a wall of colored holds.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard someone yell, ‘Almost there!’","heat":1},{"text":"I heard rubber shoes squeak against the wall.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard a belayer call, ‘Take!’ from below.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a child embarrass three adults.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a woman reach for a tiny red grip.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a belayer manage rope below a climber.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a water bottle covered in dust.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a chalk bag beside the padded floor.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a harness with dangling carabiners.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my arms became spaghetti.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after failing the same yellow route.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when I couldn’t grip another hold.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was near the wall, stretching.","heat":1},{"text":"I was halfway up, refusing to look down.","heat":2},{"text":"I was dangling from a rope over the crash mats.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was pretending I wasn't tired.","heat":1},{"text":"I was chalking my hands for the fifth time.","heat":2},{"text":"I was climbing colorful holds in a harness.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-bowling-alley","pack":"party","category":"game-venues","emoji":"🎳","name":"Bowling Alley","fullName":"A Bowling Alley","clues":["A teenager celebrates wildly while the scoreboard displays an embarrassingly low number.","A thunderous crash is followed by cheers from one table and groans from another.","Hot pizza, floor polish, and suspiciously clean rental shoes."],"hint":"Somewhere people compete for fun","facts":[{"en":"A perfect game in bowling scores 300 points: twelve strikes in a row."},{"en":"A standard tenpin bowling pin stands 15 inches tall."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate fries while everyone blamed me.","heat":1},{"text":"I spilled nacho cheese on my rented shoes.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate pizza beside ten stubborn wooden pins.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard a crash followed by applause.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard heavy balls rumbling down wooden lanes.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard all ten pins explode after a strike.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a grandma destroy everyone's confidence.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a kid celebrate knocking down one pin.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a staffer rescue a ball from the gutter.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried something heavier than expected.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a shoe with somebody else's name.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a shiny ball with three finger holes.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my friends started keeping score.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after seven straight gutter balls.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when the pinsetter jammed again.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was at a table with my friends.","heat":1},{"text":"I was on lane seven, losing badly.","heat":2},{"text":"I was at the ball return, picking a 12-pounder.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was keeping score. Badly.","heat":1},{"text":"I was doing my victory dance. Too early.","heat":2},{"text":"I was rolling gutter balls in rented shoes.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-mini-golf","pack":"party","category":"game-venues","emoji":"⛳","name":"Mini Golf","fullName":"A Miniature Golf Course","clues":["A tiny plastic windmill blocks the path of a bright orange ball.","A gentle tap is followed by someone accusing a decorative dinosaur of cheating.","Freshly trimmed grass, damp concrete, and nearby ice cream cones."],"hint":"Somewhere people compete for fun","facts":[{"en":"One of the first mini golf courses, 'Tom Thumb Golf', opened on Lookout Mountain, Tennessee, in 1927."},{"en":"During the 1930s mini golf craze, thousands of courses opened across the United States."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate candy while plotting my comeback.","heat":1},{"text":"I dropped popcorn beside a tiny waterfall.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate a hot dog near the spinning windmill.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard someone yell, 'That doesn't count!'","heat":1},{"text":"I heard a little ball rattle inside a tunnel.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard my ball bounce off a plastic castle.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I watched a child defeat three adults.","heat":1},{"text":"I saw a couple argue over a crooked shot.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a kid putt beneath a giant windmill.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a pencil with no eraser.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a bright orange ball in the bushes.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a tiny putter and a scorecard.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left after losing to a seven-year-old.","heat":1},{"text":"I left when my ball vanished into the pond.","heat":2},{"text":"I left after the final hole swallowed my ball.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was outside, near the entrance.","heat":1},{"text":"I was stuck on hole nine for ten minutes.","heat":2},{"text":"I was next to the windmill, losing to it.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was keeping score with a tiny pencil.","heat":1},{"text":"I was arguing about a do-over.","heat":2},{"text":"I was putting a neon ball past a fake dinosaur.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-laser-tag","pack":"party","category":"game-venues","emoji":"🔫","name":"Laser Tag","fullName":"A Laser Tag Arena","clues":["Glowing red and blue vests dart between futuristic barriers in a dark maze.","Electronic blasts, dramatic battle music, and someone yelling that their equipment is broken.","Artificial fog, plastic equipment, and warm carpet."],"hint":"Somewhere people compete for fun","facts":[{"en":"The first laser tag arena, Photon, opened in Dallas, Texas, in 1984."},{"en":"Most laser tag guns don't use lasers at all: they fire invisible infrared light."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate chips while planning revenge.","heat":1},{"text":"I drank water beneath glowing purple lights.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate pizza after returning my glowing vest.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard somebody scream, 'Behind you!'","heat":1},{"text":"I heard electronic blasts echo in the dark.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard my sensor beep after another hit.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a quiet kid become terrifying.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a teenager hide behind a glowing wall.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a staffer adjust someone's flashing vest.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried something that made me feel powerful.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a glowing wristband behind a barrier.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a plastic blaster with a red sensor.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my team stopped trusting me.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after hiding in the same corner twice.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when the arena lights came back on.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was somewhere dark.","heat":1},{"text":"I was hiding behind a glowing wall.","heat":2},{"text":"I was crouched in the maze in a light-up vest.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was running around a lot.","heat":1},{"text":"I was ambushing my best friend. No regrets.","heat":2},{"text":"I was firing a laser at the red team.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-arcade","pack":"party","category":"game-venues","emoji":"🕹️","name":"Arcade","fullName":"A Retro Video Game Arcade","clues":["Rows of flashing cabinets surround a child proudly holding an enormous pile of paper tickets.","Electronic jingles, rapid button tapping, and the triumphant scream of someone winning a stuffed banana.","Warm electronics, sugary drinks, and buttery popcorn."],"hint":"Somewhere people compete for fun","facts":[{"en":"Atari's Pong, released in 1972, was one of the first hit arcade video games."},{"en":"Pac-Man was originally released in Japan as 'Puck-Man'."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate candy and regretted sharing.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate fries beneath a thousand blinking lights.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate pizza beside a mountain of prize tickets.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard somebody shout, 'One more try!'","heat":1},{"text":"I heard electronic jingles fighting for attention.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard coins drop and a jackpot siren wail.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a child negotiate like a lawyer.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a teenager defeat a dancing machine.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a kid trade 900 tickets for a pencil.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a plastic dinosaur with one eye.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a forgotten token beneath a machine.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a card loaded with game credits.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my wallet surrendered.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after losing to the claw machine again.","heat":2},{"text":"I left with 400 tickets and a rubber spider.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was by the snack machines.","heat":1},{"text":"I was in a corner full of flashing lights.","heat":2},{"text":"I was at the prize counter with too few tickets.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was playing a few games.","heat":1},{"text":"I was mashing buttons and losing to a kid.","heat":2},{"text":"I was feeding tokens into a claw machine.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-escape-room","pack":"party","category":"game-venues","emoji":"🔐","name":"Escape Room","fullName":"An Escape Room","clues":["Four adults argue over a mysterious wooden box while a giant countdown glows red.","A mechanical click interrupts someone shouting that they have solved everything.","Dusty furniture, artificial fog, and somebody's stress-induced perspiration."],"hint":"Somewhere people compete for fun","facts":[{"en":"The first live escape room game is usually credited to SCRAP in Kyoto, Japan, in 2007."},{"en":"Many escape rooms give teams 60 minutes to solve the puzzles and get out."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate a cookie while blaming my teammates.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate candy after solving a stubborn riddle.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate pizza after our locked-door countdown ended.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard someone whisper, 'Don't touch that.'","heat":1},{"text":"I heard a hidden latch click behind a painting.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard the final countdown over a locked door.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw my smartest friend panic over a number.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a teammate inspect every fake book.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw our game master offer a cryptic clue.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a key that opened absolutely nothing.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a coded message beneath a loose tile.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a four-digit lock and a cipher wheel.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when everyone blamed my math.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after our final clue made no sense.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when the game master ended our timer.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was in a small themed room.","heat":1},{"text":"I was by the door that wouldn't open.","heat":2},{"text":"I was next to the giant countdown clock.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was solving a puzzle. Allegedly.","heat":1},{"text":"I was yelling 'try 1-2-3-4!' at everyone.","heat":2},{"text":"I was hunting for the key to a locked box.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-karaoke-bar","pack":"party","category":"show-venues","emoji":"🎤","name":"Karaoke Bar","fullName":"A Karaoke Bar","clues":["A nervous man grips a microphone while his friends wave glowing plastic sticks.","Someone confidently performs an entire chorus in the wrong key.","Fried appetizers, spilled soda, and an aggressively floral air freshener."],"hint":"Somewhere with an audience","facts":[{"en":"'Karaoke' is Japanese for 'empty orchestra': the music plays without a singer."},{"en":"Daisuke Inoue built an early karaoke machine in Japan in 1971 and never patented it."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate fries to avoid answering questions.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate nachos while my friend butchered a chorus.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate wings beside a screen full of song lyrics.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard a note that frightened the furniture.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard a crowd rescue a forgotten chorus.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard a microphone squeal between two songs.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw my shy friend become a superstar.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a couple argue over a duet.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw the host hand a microphone to a stranger.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a napkin covered in nervous scribbles.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a song-request slip beneath my chair.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a wireless microphone onto the stage.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my confidence ran out.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after my duet partner forgot every word.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when the host announced the final song.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was at a table near the back.","heat":1},{"text":"I was right next to the speakers.","heat":2},{"text":"I was on the tiny stage holding the mic.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was having a drink with friends.","heat":1},{"text":"I was cheering for someone very off-key.","heat":2},{"text":"I was belting a power ballad off a screen.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-comedy-club","pack":"party","category":"show-venues","emoji":"🎙️","name":"Comedy Club","fullName":"A Stand-Up Comedy Club","clues":["A single spotlight illuminates a nervous performer while the front row avoids eye contact.","A room erupts in laughter, followed by an uncomfortable silence after a terrible joke.","Fresh nachos, citrus soda, and a little too much cologne."],"hint":"Somewhere with an audience","facts":[{"en":"The Comedy Store, one of the most famous comedy clubs, opened in Los Angeles in 1972."},{"en":"Many comedians test new jokes at small 'open mic' nights before using them in big shows."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate fries while pretending to understand.","heat":1},{"text":"I choked on popcorn during an awkward punchline.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate nachos beneath a tiny brick-wall stage.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard one person laugh three seconds late.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard nervous laughter after a terrible joke.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard a microphone drop after the final punchline.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a man regret sitting in front.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a performer roast someone's haircut.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw the emcee introduce a nervous stand-up act.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a napkin covered in bad ideas.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a crumpled set list near the stage.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a crumpled ticket that said 'Front Row'.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left before somebody noticed my face.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after becoming the punchline twice.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when the final comedian dropped the mic.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was sitting in the dark.","heat":1},{"text":"I was at a tiny table near the wall.","heat":2},{"text":"I was in the front row. Big mistake.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was laughing politely.","heat":1},{"text":"I was trying not to make eye contact.","heat":2},{"text":"I was getting roasted by the comedian.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-haunted-house","pack":"party","category":"show-venues","emoji":"👻","name":"Haunted House","fullName":"A Haunted House Attraction","clues":["A crooked portrait appears to follow visitors with its eyes while a plastic skeleton hangs from the ceiling.","A sudden scream is followed by someone insisting they were not frightened.","Artificial fog, dusty curtains, and cinnamon from a nearby snack stand."],"hint":"Somewhere with an audience","facts":[{"en":"Disneyland's Haunted Mansion opened in 1969."},{"en":"Haunted attractions often hire 'scare actors' whose whole job is to make visitors jump."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate candy to recover my dignity.","heat":1},{"text":"I dropped my popcorn when something grabbed me.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate gummy worms beside a fake spider the size of a cat.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard someone scream louder than me.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard chains dragging behind a dark curtain.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard a fake chainsaw roar beside a coffin.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a teenager hide behind his little sister.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a masked actor crawl from the shadows.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a zombie performer chase our entire group.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a flashlight with dying batteries.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a plastic bone beneath a curtain.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a rubber skull past a fake grave.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my courage abandoned me.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after a masked stranger jumped out.","heat":2},{"text":"I left through the emergency exit by the coffins.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was somewhere very dark.","heat":1},{"text":"I was in a hallway full of fake cobwebs.","heat":2},{"text":"I was behind my friend, next to a fake coffin.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was walking very slowly.","heat":1},{"text":"I was screaming and pretending I wasn't.","heat":2},{"text":"I was running from a guy with a chainsaw.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-magic-show","pack":"party","category":"show-venues","emoji":"🎩","name":"Magic Show","fullName":"A Live Magic Show","clues":["A volunteer stares suspiciously at an empty hat while the performer smiles confidently.","Dramatic music builds before the audience gasps at something nobody can explain.","Velvet curtains, stage makeup, and freshly popped corn."],"hint":"Somewhere with an audience","facts":[{"en":"Harry Houdini, the famous escape artist, was born Erik Weisz in Budapest in 1874."},{"en":"The magic word 'abracadabra' dates back to ancient Rome, where it was written on charms."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate popcorn while questioning reality.","heat":1},{"text":"I spilled soda when something vanished.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate candy as a rabbit emerged from a hat.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard a gasp followed by suspicious applause.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard a drumroll before an empty box opened.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard the crowd gasp at a floating assistant.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a volunteer regret raising his hand.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a performer make someone's watch vanish.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a magician pull silk scarves from thin air.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a card I wasn't allowed to show.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a silk scarf beneath the front row.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a signed playing card from a trick.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my brain demanded an explanation.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after the performer guessed my secret card.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when the magician vanished behind a curtain.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was in a seat in the middle.","heat":1},{"text":"I was close enough to see up the sleeves.","heat":2},{"text":"I was on stage as the volunteer.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was clapping a lot.","heat":1},{"text":"I was trying to figure out the trick.","heat":2},{"text":"I was picking a card. Any card.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-all-you-can-eat-buffet","pack":"party","category":"food-venues","emoji":"🍽️","name":"The Buffet","fullName":"An All-You-Can-Eat Buffet","clues":["A man balances an impossible mountain of mashed potatoes, noodles, and three desserts on a single plate.","Metal serving spoons clatter against trays while someone announces they're going back for a fourth round.","Roasted chicken, warm bread, and approximately twelve different cuisines competing for attention."],"hint":"Somewhere people go when they're hungry","facts":[{"en":"The word buffet comes from French, where it originally meant a sideboard for serving food."},{"en":"Las Vegas casinos helped popularize the all-you-can-eat buffet in the 1940s."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate dessert before anyone noticed.","heat":1},{"text":"I stacked three desserts beside my mashed potatoes.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate shrimp from the fourth serving station.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard someone whisper, 'Just one more.'","heat":1},{"text":"I heard serving tongs clatter against metal trays.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard plates stack beside the endless food line.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a grandpa make a questionable decision.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a kid carry a mountain of desserts.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a staffer refill the empty carving station.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried something heavier than expected.","heat":1},{"text":"I carried a plate with six different desserts.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a fresh plate back for my third helping.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my stomach requested mercy.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after promising not to get fourths.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when they cleared the last serving station.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was at a big table near the window.","heat":1},{"text":"I was in the dessert line. Again.","heat":2},{"text":"I was guarding the chocolate fountain.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was eating. A lot.","heat":1},{"text":"I was loosening my belt between plates.","heat":2},{"text":"I was going back for my fifth plate.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-fancy-restaurant","pack":"party","category":"food-venues","emoji":"🥂","name":"Fancy Restaurant","fullName":"An Extremely Fancy Restaurant","clues":["A waiter presents a plate containing one tiny carrot surrounded by an artistic arrangement of mysterious green dots.","Silverware gently touches expensive plates while someone quietly asks which fork they're supposed to use.","Truffle oil, freshly baked bread, and perfume that probably costs more than dinner."],"hint":"Somewhere people go when they're hungry","facts":[{"en":"The Michelin Guide was first published in 1900 by a tire company to encourage people to drive more."},{"en":"Michelin began awarding its famous restaurant stars in 1926."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate something tiny and pretended to be full.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate a flower that apparently counted as garnish.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate three scallops arranged with edible flowers.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard someone whisper about the price.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard silverware tap against delicate plates.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard a server describe twelve tasting courses.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a man pretend he understood everything.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a server fold a napkin like origami.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a chef present a dish beneath a glass dome.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a napkin I was afraid to stain.","heat":1},{"text":"I found three forks beside my dinner plate.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a tiny spoon for an even tinier course.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my wallet started sweating.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after the seventh mysterious little plate.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when the server presented the final petit four.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was at a quiet table.","heat":1},{"text":"I was under a chandelier, feeling poor.","heat":2},{"text":"I was at a white tablecloth with six forks.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was on my best behavior.","heat":1},{"text":"I was pretending to understand the wine list.","heat":2},{"text":"I was waiting for course nine of twelve.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-food-truck-festival","pack":"party","category":"food-venues","emoji":"🚚","name":"Food Truck Festival","fullName":"A Food Truck Festival","clues":["A dozen colorful vehicles line a parking lot while a man struggles to carry tacos, fries, and an enormous lemonade.","Generators hum beneath cheerful conversations and someone shouting that order number forty-seven is ready.","Grilled onions, smoky barbecue, and freshly fried dough drift through the afternoon air."],"hint":"Somewhere people go when they're hungry","facts":[{"en":"Rancher Charles Goodnight created the chuck wagon in 1866 to feed cowboys on cattle drives."},{"en":"Modern gourmet food trucks took off in Los Angeles around 2008, led by Kogi BBQ's Korean tacos."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate something messy with both hands.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate tacos while standing beside a smoky grill.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate loaded fries from a brightly painted truck.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard someone shout, 'Order up!'","heat":1},{"text":"I heard generators humming beneath live music.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard five truck kitchens calling order numbers.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a kid wearing more sauce than shirt.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a cook flip tortillas through a window.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw families queue between rows of mobile kitchens.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a napkin that surrendered immediately.","heat":1},{"text":"I carried three cardboard trays stacked together.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried numbered tickets from two different trucks.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my shirt became a menu.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after standing in my fourth food line.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when the last truck closed its serving window.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was outside, near a parking lot.","heat":1},{"text":"I was in a line that went around the block.","heat":2},{"text":"I was between a taco truck and a crêpe van.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was trying a bit of everything.","heat":1},{"text":"I was juggling three plates and a lemonade.","heat":2},{"text":"I was ordering through a truck window.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-ice-cream-parlor","pack":"party","category":"food-venues","emoji":"🍦","name":"Ice Cream Parlor","fullName":"An Ice Cream Parlor","clues":["A little girl watches in horror as a towering pink dessert slowly slides toward the floor.","Metal scoops scrape against frozen containers while someone debates whether sprinkles count as a vegetable.","Sweet vanilla, warm waffle cones, and melted chocolate."],"hint":"Somewhere people go when they're hungry","facts":[{"en":"The ice cream cone became famous at the 1904 World's Fair in St. Louis."},{"en":"Italian gelato usually has less air whipped into it than American ice cream, so it tastes denser."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate dessert faster than I should have.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate something cold with rainbow sprinkles.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate three scoops from a waffle cone.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard a child shout, 'That's not fair!'","heat":1},{"text":"I heard metal scoops scrape against frozen tubs.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard the freezer hum behind thirty flavors.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a dad negotiate with a five-year-old.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a kid sample six flavors before choosing.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a server balance four scoops on one cone.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a sticky napkin like evidence.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a tiny sample spoon under my chair.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a waffle cone dripping onto my shoes.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my hands became sticky.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after losing half my dessert to gravity.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when my last scoop melted through the cone.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was at a little table by the window.","heat":1},{"text":"I was at the counter, tasting samples.","heat":2},{"text":"I was in front of 32 frozen flavors.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was treating myself.","heat":1},{"text":"I was asking for a sixth tiny sample spoon.","heat":2},{"text":"I was licking a drip off a waffle cone.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-sushi-conveyor-belt","pack":"party","category":"food-venues","emoji":"🍣","name":"Sushi Train","fullName":"A Conveyor Belt Sushi Restaurant","clues":["Tiny colorful plates glide past a family while a child desperately waits for the one with the orange topping.","Dishes click gently along a moving track as someone announces that their favorite plate has escaped again.","Steamed rice, soy sauce, and freshly prepared seafood."],"hint":"Somewhere people go when they're hungry","facts":[{"en":"Conveyor belt sushi was invented in Osaka, Japan, in 1958, inspired by a beer-bottling conveyor."},{"en":"Sushi began as a way to preserve fish by packing it in fermented rice."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate something I couldn't pronounce.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate salmon rolls from a passing little plate.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate tuna nigiri from a moving belt.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard someone yell, 'Grab that one!'","heat":1},{"text":"I heard little dishes clink as they passed.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard the plate-return slot count our dishes.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a kid make a terrible choice.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a woman chase her favorite dish.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a chef load fresh rolls onto the moving belt.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried something small and surprisingly expensive.","heat":1},{"text":"I found an empty plate stacked beside my elbow.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a color-coded plate from the moving belt.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my friends counted my mistakes.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after stacking twelve little dishes.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when the plate counter reached twenty.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was at a counter seat.","heat":1},{"text":"I was in a booth with a stack of plates.","heat":2},{"text":"I was right next to the moving belt.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was eating something small and fancy.","heat":1},{"text":"I was stacking colorful plates like trophies.","heat":2},{"text":"I was grabbing plates as they rolled past.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-airport-security","pack":"party","category":"travel-venues","emoji":"🛂","name":"Airport Security","fullName":"An Airport Security Checkpoint","clues":["A businessman stands barefoot beside a mountain of plastic bins while searching desperately for his laptop.","Electronic beeps interrupt instructions to remove jackets and empty pockets.","Fresh coffee, cleaning products, and the unmistakable scent of hundreds of hurried travelers."],"hint":"Somewhere people pass through on a journey","facts":[{"en":"Airline passenger screening became mandatory in the United States in 1973."},{"en":"Airport codes like LAX or JFK use three letters assigned by the International Air Transport Association (IATA)."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate a granola bar while standing in line.","heat":1},{"text":"I finished my snack before the bag inspection.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate crackers after surrendering my water bottle.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard someone sigh louder than necessary.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard plastic bins rattling along metal rollers.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard the body scanner beep beside the checkpoint.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a dad searching every pocket.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a traveler remove a forgotten belt.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a screening officer inspect a crowded tray.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a bag that weighed too much.","heat":1},{"text":"I carried my shoes in a gray plastic bin.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a boarding pass past the X-ray machine.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when the line finally moved.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after they inspected my backpack twice.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when my carry-on cleared the X-ray belt.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was in a long line.","heat":1},{"text":"I was standing around in my socks.","heat":2},{"text":"I was in the body scanner, arms up.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was waiting. And waiting.","heat":1},{"text":"I was taking my belt off in public.","heat":2},{"text":"I was putting my laptop in a gray plastic bin.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-cruise-ship","pack":"party","category":"travel-venues","emoji":"🛳️","name":"Cruise Ship","fullName":"A Cruise Ship at Sea","clues":["An elderly couple dances beside a swimming pool while a waiter carefully navigates around a tower of tropical drinks.","Distant music blends with splashing water and an announcement about tonight's entertainment.","Salty ocean air, sunscreen, and freshly grilled burgers."],"hint":"Somewhere people pass through on a journey","facts":[{"en":"'Starboard', the right side of a ship, comes from the 'steering board' old ships carried on that side."},{"en":"The largest cruise ships today carry more than 5,000 passengers."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate dessert before lunch. Nobody objected.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate shrimp while watching the horizon move.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate pancakes beside a pool above the ocean.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard music and somebody cheering.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard waves slap beneath the dining windows.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard the captain announce our next port.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a grandpa dancing without permission.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a family pose against endless blue water.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a crew member lead games beside the upper pool.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a towel that wasn't mine.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a room key beside a lounge chair.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a cabin keycard onto the upper deck.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when the sun became unbearable.","heat":1},{"text":"I left the pool when the waves got rough.","heat":2},{"text":"I left at the final port with my cabin luggage.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was outside, enjoying the view.","heat":1},{"text":"I was by the pool on a lounge chair.","heat":2},{"text":"I was on the top deck, staring at the ocean.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was relaxing. Very hard.","heat":1},{"text":"I was at the all-night buffet. Again.","heat":2},{"text":"I was waving at dolphins from the railing.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-overnight-train","pack":"party","category":"travel-venues","emoji":"🚆","name":"Sleeper Train","fullName":"An Overnight Sleeper Train","clues":["A passenger attempts to climb into a tiny upper bed while another watches the countryside disappear into darkness.","A steady metallic rhythm accompanies the occasional rattle of cups on a narrow table.","Warm blankets, instant noodles, and freshly brewed tea."],"hint":"Somewhere people pass through on a journey","facts":[{"en":"George Pullman's sleeping cars made overnight train travel comfortable in the 1860s."},{"en":"The Orient Express first ran from Paris to Constantinople (now Istanbul) in 1883."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate a sandwich at a ridiculous hour.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate noodles while the table gently rattled.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate breakfast in a dining car before sunrise.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard somebody snoring through the wall.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard wheels click rhythmically beneath my bed.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard the conductor announce our next station.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a stranger sleeping with one shoe on.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a passenger unfold a tiny upper bunk.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw a conductor check tickets beside the sleeper cabins.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a pillow that smelled like soap.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a blanket folded beneath a narrow bunk.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a ticket with my sleeper berth number.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left because sleeping had become impossible.","heat":1},{"text":"I left my bunk when the sunrise filled the window.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when the conductor called our morning stop.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was by a window.","heat":1},{"text":"I was in a narrow hallway, swaying.","heat":2},{"text":"I was in a tiny bunk, top level.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was trying to sleep.","heat":1},{"text":"I was watching dark fields roll by.","heat":2},{"text":"I was climbing a ladder into my sleeper bed.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-crowded-subway","pack":"party","category":"travel-venues","emoji":"🚇","name":"Subway Station","fullName":"A Crowded Subway Station","clues":["A businessman squeezes between commuters while a street musician performs beside a brightly colored map.","A deep rumble approaches as an automated voice announces the next arrival.","Warm concrete, strong coffee, and somebody's breakfast sandwich."],"hint":"Somewhere people pass through on a journey","facts":[{"en":"The world's first underground railway opened in London in 1863."},{"en":"At rush hour, some Tokyo stations have used staff called 'oshiya' to gently push passengers onto packed trains."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate a granola bar while standing.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate a pretzel squeezed between two backpacks.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate a snack while gripping a swaying handrail.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard someone complain about the delay.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard metal wheels screech around a sharp curve.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard the doors chime before the next station.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a man sleeping through absolute chaos.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched three commuters fight for one empty seat.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw passengers squeeze through closing train doors.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a backpack against my chest.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a transit card beside the metal pole.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a folded route map beneath the handrail.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when I couldn't stand another minute.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after missing my stop in the crowd.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when the doors opened at my transfer station.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was underground, I think.","heat":1},{"text":"I was on the platform behind the yellow line.","heat":2},{"text":"I was pressed against the doors of a packed train.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was going home.","heat":1},{"text":"I was reading a map nobody understands.","heat":2},{"text":"I was holding a pole with 40 strangers.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-kids-birthday","pack":"party","category":"celebrations","emoji":"🎂","name":"Kids' Birthday Party","fullName":"A Chaotic Children's Birthday Party","clues":["A child wearing a paper crown cries because someone else received a larger slice of cake.","Fifteen children scream different instructions while an exhausted adult attempts to organize a group photograph.","Chocolate frosting, cheese pizza, and fruit punch spilled somewhere nobody can find."],"hint":"Somewhere people gather for a special occasion","facts":[{"en":"The 'Happy Birthday' melody comes from 'Good Morning to All', published by sisters Mildred and Patty Hill in 1893."},{"en":"Piñatas are traditionally broken at Mexican celebrations like birthdays and Christmas posadas."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate something before anyone said I could.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate pizza while six kids fought over balloons.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate cake with blue frosting and dinosaur sprinkles.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard someone shout, 'That's mine!'","heat":1},{"text":"I heard children screaming over a wrapped box.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard twenty kids sing around a candlelit cake.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a dad hiding behind the furniture.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched a child cry over the wrong balloon.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw the birthday kid attack a mountain of gifts.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a bag full of mysterious crumbs.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a paper crown beneath the snack table.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a gift wrapped in dinosaur paper.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when the noise defeated me.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after the third balloon exploded.","heat":2},{"text":"I left when every kid received a party favor.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was in a living room.","heat":1},{"text":"I was hiding in the kitchen.","heat":2},{"text":"I was next to the bouncy castle.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was helping out. Sort of.","heat":1},{"text":"I was breaking up a fight over balloons.","heat":2},{"text":"I was singing to a very sticky birthday kid.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-wedding-reception","pack":"party","category":"celebrations","emoji":"💒","name":"Wedding Reception","fullName":"A Wedding Reception","clues":["An uncle wearing an extremely shiny suit performs dance moves nobody requested.","Glasses clink as someone begins a speech that was clearly supposed to last two minutes.","Fresh flowers, roasted vegetables, and an impressive amount of hairspray."],"hint":"Somewhere people gather for a special occasion","facts":[{"en":"The wedding 'toast' is named after an old custom of putting a piece of spiced toast in drinks for flavor."},{"en":"Some couples save the top tier of their wedding cake to eat on their first anniversary."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate dessert before the main course.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate chicken while strangers clinked their glasses.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate a slice of three-tiered white cake.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard someone crying happy tears.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard a crowd cheer during a slow dance.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard the DJ announce the newlyweds' first dance.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw an uncle dancing without rhythm.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched two families pose for endless photos.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw the couple cut a towering white cake.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a napkin covered in cake frosting.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a tiny flower bouquet beneath a chair.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a place card with the couple's initials.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left when my dancing shoes surrendered.","heat":1},{"text":"I left after the fourth emotional speech.","heat":2},{"text":"I left after the couple's final dance.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was at a round table.","heat":1},{"text":"I was on the dance floor. Against my will.","heat":2},{"text":"I was at table 12, right behind the cake.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was having a nice time.","heat":1},{"text":"I was crying during the speeches.","heat":2},{"text":"I was catching the bouquet. By accident.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-graduation-ceremony","pack":"party","category":"celebrations","emoji":"🎓","name":"Graduation","fullName":"A Graduation Ceremony","clues":["Hundreds of people wear identical outfits while one proud grandmother waves a homemade sign the size of a refrigerator.","Polite applause turns into deafening cheering when someone shouts a familiar name.","Fresh flowers, warm fabric, and the faint aroma of coffee from exhausted relatives."],"hint":"Somewhere people gather for a special occasion","facts":[{"en":"The flat graduation cap is called a mortarboard because it looks like a mason's board for holding mortar."},{"en":"At many US graduations, graduates move their tassel from right to left once they've graduated."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate a cookie while waiting for everyone.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate cupcakes decorated with tiny black hats.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate cake shaped like a rolled diploma.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard somebody cheer much too loudly.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard hundreds of names read into a microphone.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard the crowd roar as tassels were moved.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a grandma crying into her phone.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched students straighten their matching gowns.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw graduates toss square caps into the air.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried flowers that kept poking my face.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a loose tassel beneath a folding chair.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a rolled diploma tied with a ribbon.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left after taking forty-seven photographs.","heat":1},{"text":"I left when the final student's name was called.","heat":2},{"text":"I left after the last cap landed on the lawn.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was sitting in a big crowd.","heat":1},{"text":"I was in the bleachers with a huge sign.","heat":2},{"text":"I was in a cap and gown, row 30.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was clapping a lot.","heat":1},{"text":"I was waiting for one specific name.","heat":2},{"text":"I was throwing my cap in the air.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"party-surprise-retirement","pack":"party","category":"celebrations","emoji":"🎉","name":"Retirement Party","fullName":"A Surprise Retirement Party","clues":["A confused older gentleman enters a decorated office while thirty coworkers leap out from behind furniture.","A chorus of surprised laughter erupts before someone begins telling an embarrassing story from twenty years ago.","Sheet cake, fresh coffee, and the familiar scent of office carpet."],"hint":"Somewhere people gather for a special occasion","facts":[{"en":"In 1889, Germany under Otto von Bismarck created one of the first national old-age pension systems."},{"en":"In the US, full Social Security retirement age is 67 for people born in 1960 or later."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"I ate cake while pretending nothing was happening.","heat":1},{"text":"I ate sandwiches beneath a banner full of jokes.","heat":2},{"text":"I ate cake shaped like an alarm clock.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"I heard everyone shout at the same time.","heat":1},{"text":"I heard coworkers laugh at thirty-year-old stories.","heat":2},{"text":"I heard 'Surprise!' followed by a farewell speech.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"I saw a manager hiding behind a curtain.","heat":1},{"text":"I watched coworkers present a framed group photo.","heat":2},{"text":"I saw the guest of honor unwrap a fishing rod.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"I carried a card covered in signatures.","heat":1},{"text":"I found a banner hidden behind the office printer.","heat":2},{"text":"I carried a plaque celebrating forty years of work.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"I left after everyone finished telling stories.","heat":1},{"text":"I left when the farewell slideshow ended.","heat":2},{"text":"I left after the retiree made one final speech.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"I was in an office.","heat":1},{"text":"I was hiding behind a desk.","heat":2},{"text":"I was crouched behind the copy machine.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"I was eating cake.","heat":1},{"text":"I was signing a giant card.","heat":2},{"text":"I was yelling 'SURPRISE!' at a confused man.","heat":3}]}},{"id":"espanol-zocalo-ciudad-mexico","pack":"espanol","category":"ciudades","emoji":"🇲🇽","name":"El Zócalo","fullName":"El Zócalo de Ciudad de México un domingo","clues":["Un niño persigue una burbuja gigante frente a la Catedral Metropolitana mientras su padre intenta tomar una foto. La burbuja explota justo cuando el padre sonríe. El detective sospecha que el niño considera esto una victoria.","Una campana de la catedral suena sobre la plaza. Un vendedor ofrece globos de colores y una familia discute si todavía tiene tiempo para visitar el Palacio Nacional. La abuela ya decidió que primero van a comer.","El olor de los esquites calientes llega desde un puesto cercano. Una señora sostiene un vaso de maíz con limón y chile mientras busca una servilleta. El viento se lleva la primera que encuentra, y el detective empieza a investigar al sospechoso invisible."],"hint":"Un lugar donde las calles cuentan historias y siempre hay algo que descubrir","facts":[{"es":"La plaza principal de Ciudad de México se llama oficialmente Plaza de la Constitución.","en":"Mexico City's main square is officially called Plaza de la Constitución (Constitution Square)."},{"es":"La Catedral Metropolitana comenzó a construirse en 1573 y tardó más de dos siglos en completarse.","en":"Construction of the Metropolitan Cathedral began in 1573 and took more than two centuries to finish."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí maíz caliente y me quemé la lengua.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí esquites con limón y mucho chile.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí esquites frente a la Catedral Metropolitana.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché una campana que tapó mi conversación.","heat":1},{"text":"Escuché las campanas de una catedral enorme.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché las campanas junto al Palacio Nacional.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a un niño perseguir una burbuja gigante.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi una bandera tan grande como mi edificio.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi la bandera gigante en la Plaza de la Constitución.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba un mapa que el viento dobló por mí.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba una foto del Palacio Nacional.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una guía del antiguo centro mexica.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui porque mis zapatos ya pedían descanso.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui cuando empezó a llover sobre la plaza.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui cuando bajaron la bandera monumental.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en una plaza muy grande.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba cerca de unos vendedores de globos.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba frente a la Catedral Metropolitana.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba paseando con mi familia.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba persiguiendo una burbuja gigante.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba viendo cómo bajaban la bandera enorme.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"la plaza","en":"square"},{"es":"la campana","en":"bell"},{"es":"la burbuja","en":"bubble"},{"es":"la bandera","en":"flag"},{"es":"los esquites","en":"corn cups with lime and chili"}],"nameEn":"Mexico City's Zócalo on a Sunday"},{"id":"espanol-mercado-oaxaca","pack":"espanol","category":"ciudades","emoji":"🌶️","name":"Mercado de Oaxaca","fullName":"Un mercado tradicional en Oaxaca","clues":["Una vendedora coloca chapulines tostados junto a bolsas de chiles secos. Un visitante observa los insectos con mucha curiosidad, pero mantiene una distancia respetable. El detective anota que el valor cambia cuando la comida tiene patas.","Una mujer pregunta el precio de una canasta mientras un cocinero golpea una tortilla contra el comal. Al fondo, alguien llama a su hijo para que deje de mirar los dulces. El niño responde que está haciendo una investigación importante.","El aroma del chocolate caliente se mezcla con el de las tlayudas que se tuestan sobre el comal. Un cliente se termina su taza de chocolate, mira el pan que todavía tiene en la bolsa y pide otra taza. El detective comprende que algunas investigaciones requieren repetir la prueba."],"hint":"Un lugar donde las calles cuentan historias y siempre hay algo que descubrir","facts":[{"es":"Oaxaca es conocida por su gran variedad de tradiciones culinarias y por sus diferentes tipos de mole.","en":"Oaxaca is known for its wide variety of food traditions and its many types of mole."},{"es":"Los chapulines tostados forman parte de la alimentación tradicional de varias comunidades de Oaxaca.","en":"Toasted grasshoppers (chapulines) are part of the traditional diet of several communities in Oaxaca."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí algo crujiente y pedí otra porción.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí una tlayuda más grande que mi plato.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí chapulines tostados y pedí agua.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché a dos vendedores discutir un precio.","heat":1},{"text":"Escuché tortillas caer sobre un comal caliente.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché el comal junto a las tlayudas.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi canastas de colores hasta el techo.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi montones de chiles secos y chocolate.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi siete tipos de mole en un solo puesto.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba una bolsa que terminó demasiado llena.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba una bolsa de mole para mi familia.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba chocolate para preparar con agua caliente.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui porque ya no podía cargar mis compras.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui cuando el humo me hizo llorar.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui con una tlayuda que no cabía en mi bolsa.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en un pasillo con muchos puestos.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba entre bolsas de chiles secos.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba frente a un puesto de chapulines.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba comprando algo para comer.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba regateando por unas especias.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba probando un chapulín. Uno solo.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"los chapulines","en":"grasshoppers"},{"es":"el comal","en":"griddle"},{"es":"el puesto","en":"market stall"},{"es":"regatear","en":"to haggle"},{"es":"la canasta","en":"basket"}],"nameEn":"A traditional market in Oaxaca"},{"id":"espanol-la-boca-buenos-aires","pack":"espanol","category":"ciudades","emoji":"💃","name":"La Boca","fullName":"La Boca en Buenos Aires","clues":["Un turista intenta fotografiar tres casas pintadas de amarillo, azul y rojo mientras una pareja baila tango en la calle. El fotógrafo retrocede para mejorar el ángulo y casi se sienta sobre una caja de recuerdos. El detective recomienda mirar detrás antes de buscar la foto perfecta.","Un músico toca el bandoneón, un instrumento parecido a un acordeón pequeño, mientras los bailarines marcan el ritmo sobre la acera. Un niño pregunta si él también puede aprender a bailar. Una bailarina le toma la mano y, en un minuto, ya está recibiendo su primera clase. Su padre apenas alcanza a sacar la cámara.","El olor de las empanadas recién horneadas sale de un pequeño restaurante. Un visitante guarda su cámara y muerde una empanada de carne, pero el relleno está tan caliente que se quema la lengua. El detective identifica al principal sospechoso: la falta de paciencia."],"hint":"Un lugar donde las calles cuentan historias y siempre hay algo que descubrir","facts":[{"es":"La Boca es un barrio de Buenos Aires conocido por sus casas de colores y su historia de inmigración.","en":"La Boca is a Buenos Aires neighborhood known for its colorful houses and its history of immigration."},{"es":"Caminito es una calle museo famosa por sus edificios pintados y sus espectáculos artísticos.","en":"Caminito is a street-museum famous for its painted buildings and street performances."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí una empanada y quemé mi lengua.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí empanadas frente a casas de colores.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí empanadas cerca de Caminito.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché música mientras buscaba mi cámara.","heat":1},{"text":"Escuché un bandoneón en plena calle.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché tango junto a las casas de chapa pintada.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi una casa pintada de tres colores.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi una pareja bailar sobre la acera.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi bailarines frente a los balcones de colores.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba zapatos cómodos para caminar.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba una foto de una calle muy colorida.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una camiseta azul y amarilla.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui cuando empezó a soplar viento frío.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui cuando empezó la siguiente clase de tango.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui cuando cerraron los puestos de Caminito.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en una calle llena de turistas.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba frente a casas de muchos colores.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba en Caminito, junto a una pareja de tango.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba tomando fotos.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba retrocediendo para que saliera todo.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba aplaudiendo a unos bailarines de tango.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"la acera","en":"sidewalk"},{"es":"el bandoneón","en":"tango accordion"},{"es":"el barrio","en":"neighborhood"},{"es":"pintada","en":"painted"},{"es":"los recuerdos","en":"souvenirs"}],"nameEn":"La Boca in Buenos Aires"},{"id":"espanol-plaza-mayor-madrid","pack":"espanol","category":"ciudades","emoji":"🏛️","name":"Plaza Mayor","fullName":"La Plaza Mayor de Madrid","clues":["Un camarero cruza la plaza con una bandeja de cafés mientras un turista busca la estatua de Felipe III. La encuentra en el centro, pero primero fotografía tres palomas que parecen convencidas de ser las verdaderas protagonistas.","Las tazas chocan suavemente en las mesas de una terraza. Un músico toca la guitarra bajo los arcos y una pareja discute qué calle tomar. El detective observa que ambos tienen un mapa y ninguno parece dispuesto a usarlo.","El olor de un bocadillo de calamares recién preparado sale de un restaurante cercano. Un visitante abre una servilleta para comer, pero una paloma se acerca con demasiada confianza. La investigación se convierte en una defensa del almuerzo."],"hint":"Un lugar donde las calles cuentan historias y siempre hay algo que descubrir","facts":[{"es":"La Plaza Mayor de Madrid fue construida principalmente durante el reinado de Felipe III, a comienzos del siglo XVII.","en":"Madrid's Plaza Mayor was built mainly during the reign of Philip III, in the early 17th century."},{"es":"La estatua ecuestre de Felipe III fue colocada en el centro de la plaza en 1848.","en":"The equestrian statue of Philip III was placed in the center of the square in 1848."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí un bocadillo y una paloma pidió la mitad.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí un bocadillo de calamares recién hecho.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí calamares bajo los arcos de la plaza.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché una guitarra bajo unos arcos.","heat":1},{"text":"Escuché las tazas de una terraza bajo los arcos.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché música junto a la estatua de Felipe III.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi una estatua de un hombre a caballo.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi a Felipe III montado en su caballo de bronce.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi los balcones rojos de la Casa de la Panadería.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba un mapa lleno de calles pequeñas.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba una bolsa de una tienda de recuerdos.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una foto de la estatua ecuestre.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui cuando el sol calentó demasiado.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui porque una paloma vigilaba mi almuerzo.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui por la calle de Toledo buscando churros.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en una plaza con terrazas.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba bajo unos soportales de piedra.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba junto a la estatua de Felipe III.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba tomando un café.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba buscando sitio en una terraza.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba comiendo un bocadillo de calamares.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"el bocadillo","en":"sandwich (Spain)"},{"es":"la paloma","en":"pigeon"},{"es":"la terraza","en":"outdoor café seating"},{"es":"los soportales","en":"arcades"},{"es":"la estatua","en":"statue"}],"nameEn":"Madrid's Plaza Mayor"},{"id":"espanol-cartagena-amurallada","pack":"espanol","category":"ciudades","emoji":"🌅","name":"Cartagena","fullName":"Cartagena de Indias al atardecer","clues":["Una vendedora lleva una bandeja de frutas sobre la cabeza mientras camina junto a una muralla de piedra. Un turista intenta fotografiar el sol sobre el mar, pero su sombrero sale volando. El detective registra que el viento también quiere participar en las vacaciones.","Las ruedas de un coche de caballos pasan sobre los adoquines mientras un músico toca una melodía en una esquina. Una familia pregunta cuánto falta para llegar al restaurante. El hijo menor responde que lleva preguntando lo mismo desde hace veinte minutos.","El aroma del pescado frito y las arepas de huevo llega desde una cocina cercana. Un visitante sostiene una botella de agua fría mientras busca una mesa a la sombra. El detective concluye que el calor puede resolver cualquier discusión sobre dónde cenar."],"hint":"Un lugar donde las calles cuentan historias y siempre hay algo que descubrir","facts":[{"es":"Cartagena de Indias fue fundada en 1533 y se convirtió en un importante puerto del Caribe.","en":"Cartagena de Indias was founded in 1533 and became an important Caribbean port."},{"es":"El puerto, las fortalezas y el conjunto monumental de Cartagena forman parte del Patrimonio Mundial de la UNESCO desde 1984.","en":"Cartagena's port, fortresses and historic center have been a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1984."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí pescado frito junto al mar.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí una arepa de huevo y pedí otra servilleta.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí arepa de huevo frente a la muralla.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché ruedas sobre calles de piedra.","heat":1},{"text":"Escuché música junto a las murallas antiguas.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché música cerca de la Torre del Reloj.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi balcones llenos de flores.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi una vendedora con frutas sobre la cabeza.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi balcones coloniales y vendedores de frutas.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba un sombrero que casi salió volando.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba una botella de agua casi vacía.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una foto del Castillo de San Felipe.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui porque el calor ganó la discusión.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui cuando el sol cayó detrás del mar.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui al anochecer por la Puerta del Reloj.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en una ciudad junto al mar.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba en una calle con balcones de flores.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba sobre la muralla, mirando el atardecer.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba caminando sin prisa.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba comprando fruta a una palenquera.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba fotografiando el sol sobre el Caribe.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"la muralla","en":"city wall"},{"es":"el atardecer","en":"sunset"},{"es":"los adoquines","en":"cobblestones"},{"es":"la palenquera","en":"traditional fruit vendor"},{"es":"el sombrero","en":"hat"}],"nameEn":"Cartagena de Indias at sunset"},{"id":"espanol-quinceanera","pack":"espanol","category":"vida-diaria","emoji":"👗","name":"Quinceañera","fullName":"Una fiesta de quince años","clues":["Una joven con un vestido elegante intenta bajar una escalera sin pisar la falda. Su prima sostiene el ramo de flores y su padre espera para bailar. El detective sospecha que el vestido necesita su propio equipo de seguridad.","El DJ anuncia el siguiente baile mientras los invitados aplauden. Una tía busca a tres primos para una foto familiar, pero uno está escondido detrás de la mesa de postres. El detective conoce perfectamente ese escondite.","El pastel de vainilla y las flores decorativas llenan el salón de aromas dulces. Un invitado sostiene un plato de arroz y pollo mientras observa la mesa de dulces. El detective calcula que todavía queda espacio para dos porciones de pastel."],"hint":"Un momento de la vida cotidiana con familia, amigos o vecinos","facts":[{"es":"La celebración de los quince años marca tradicionalmente una etapa importante en la vida de una joven en muchas comunidades latinoamericanas.","en":"A quinceañera traditionally marks an important stage in a young woman's life in many Latin American communities."},{"es":"Las costumbres pueden incluir un baile especial, una ceremonia religiosa o una reunión familiar, según la familia y la región.","en":"Customs can include a special dance, a religious ceremony or a family gathering, depending on the family and the region."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí pastel y escondí otra porción.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí pastel después de un baile muy elegante.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí pastel junto a quince velas decorativas.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché música hasta que me dolieron los pies.","heat":1},{"text":"Escuché al DJ anunciar un baile especial.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché anunciar el vals de la quinceañera.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a una familia tomar cien fotografías.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi un vestido enorme bajar por la escalera.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi a la festejada bailar con su padre.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba zapatos que parecían instrumentos de tortura.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba flores para la joven de la fiesta.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba un regalo para sus quince años.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui cuando mis pies pidieron ayuda.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui después del baile con su papá.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui después de la última foto familiar.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en un salón de fiestas.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba en una mesa cerca de la pista.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba junto a la escalera, esperando a la festejada.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba bailando un poco.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba aplaudiendo el vals con su padre.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba en la fila para la foto con la quinceañera.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"el pastel","en":"cake"},{"es":"el vestido","en":"dress"},{"es":"el vals","en":"waltz"},{"es":"la escalera","en":"staircase"},{"es":"la festejada","en":"guest of honor"}],"nameEn":"A quinceañera party"},{"id":"espanol-panaderia-madrugada","pack":"espanol","category":"vida-diaria","emoji":"🥐","name":"La panadería","fullName":"Una panadería a las seis de la mañana","clues":["Un panadero abre el horno y saca una bandeja de panes dulces cubiertos de azúcar. Un cliente todavía medio dormido señala tres piezas, pero el panadero entiende cinco. El detective considera que el error favorece claramente al cliente.","Una campanita suena cuando se abre la puerta. Las pinzas metálicas chocan contra una bandeja y la máquina de café comienza a trabajar. Un hombre bosteza tan fuerte que casi interrumpe el pedido de la siguiente persona.","El aroma del pan recién horneado se mezcla con canela y café caliente. Una estudiante sostiene una mochila y una bolsa de papel, pero decide salir temprano cuando descubre que el autobús está llegando."],"hint":"Un momento de la vida cotidiana con familia, amigos o vecinos","facts":[{"es":"El pan dulce tiene muchas variedades regionales en América Latina.","en":"Sweet bread (pan dulce) has many regional varieties across Latin America."},{"es":"En México existen cientos de variedades de pan dulce, muchas con nombres curiosos como orejas, besos o cuernitos.","en":"Mexico has hundreds of kinds of pan dulce, many with funny names like orejas (ears), besos (kisses) or cuernitos (little horns)."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí algo caliente y me quemé la lengua.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí pan dulce antes de que saliera el sol.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí una pieza de pan dulce recién horneada.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché una campanita al abrir la puerta.","heat":1},{"text":"Escuché bandejas metálicas salir del horno.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché al panadero sacar la primera bandeja.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a un señor bostezar frente al mostrador.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi al panadero cubierto de harina.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi el reloj marcar las seis junto al horno.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba una bolsa de papel casi vacía.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba café y una bolsa de pan caliente.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una bolsa de bolillos todavía calientes.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui porque mi autobús estaba llegando.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui cuando comenzó a formarse una fila.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui antes del amanecer con pan y café.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en una tienda pequeña.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba frente a una vitrina llena de pan.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba junto al horno, a las seis de la mañana.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba haciendo un mandado.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba eligiendo pan con pinzas y una charola.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba comprando pan dulce recién horneado.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"el panadero","en":"baker"},{"es":"el horno","en":"oven"},{"es":"las pinzas","en":"tongs"},{"es":"la charola","en":"tray (Mexico)"},{"es":"la madrugada","en":"early morning, before dawn"}],"nameEn":"A bakery at six in the morning"},{"id":"espanol-boda-mariachi","pack":"espanol","category":"vida-diaria","emoji":"🎺","name":"Boda con mariachi","fullName":"Una boda con mariachi","clues":["Los recién casados caminan entre las mesas mientras un músico con traje de charro ajusta su sombrero. Un niño lleva los anillos de recuerdo en una pequeña caja y anuncia que ahora es responsable de la seguridad de las joyas.","Las trompetas comienzan una canción alegre mientras los invitados aplauden. Una abuela reconoce la melodía y empieza a cantar antes que los músicos. El detective sospecha que ella conoce todas las canciones del repertorio.","El aroma del mole y las tortillas calientes llega desde la cocina. Un invitado sostiene una cámara y un plato al mismo tiempo, pero decide dejar de tomar fotografías cuando la salsa amenaza con caer sobre su camisa."],"hint":"Un momento de la vida cotidiana con familia, amigos o vecinos","facts":[{"es":"El mariachi es una tradición musical de México reconocida por la UNESCO como Patrimonio Cultural Inmaterial de la Humanidad desde 2011.","en":"Mariachi is a Mexican musical tradition recognized by UNESCO as Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity since 2011."},{"es":"Los grupos de mariachi modernos suelen incluir violines, trompetas, guitarras, vihuela y guitarrón.","en":"Modern mariachi groups usually include violins, trumpets, guitars, vihuela and guitarrón."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí pollo con salsa y manché mi camisa.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí mole mientras sonaban las trompetas.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí mole mientras el mariachi tocaba.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché una canción que todos conocían.","heat":1},{"text":"Escuché violines y guitarras junto a la pista.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché trompetas durante el primer baile.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a una pareja bailar entre las mesas.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi músicos con sombreros grandes y elegantes.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi a los novios bailar frente a los mariachis.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba una cámara y olvidé tomar fotos.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba un regalo para los recién casados.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una foto del grupo con trajes de charro.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui cuando mis zapatos dejaron de cooperar.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui después de una canción muy romántica.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui cuando terminó la serenata de los novios.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en una mesa redonda.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba cerca de la pista de baile.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba al lado de los mariachis.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba celebrando con la familia.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba cantando con toda el alma.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba pidiéndoles otra canción a los mariachis.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"la boda","en":"wedding"},{"es":"los recién casados","en":"newlyweds"},{"es":"los novios","en":"bride and groom"},{"es":"la trompeta","en":"trumpet"},{"es":"el traje de charro","en":"mariachi outfit"}],"nameEn":"A wedding with mariachi"},{"id":"espanol-futbol-barrio","pack":"espanol","category":"vida-diaria","emoji":"⚽","name":"Fútbol del barrio","fullName":"Un partido de fútbol del barrio","clues":["Un niño corre detrás de una pelota mientras su compañero defiende una portería marcada con dos mochilas. Un perro aparece en medio de la cancha y se lleva la pelota. El detective declara que el nuevo jugador tiene cuatro patas y ninguna intención de respetar las reglas.","Un silbato anuncia el comienzo del segundo tiempo mientras los espectadores gritan desde la sombra. Un padre asegura que el balón salió de la cancha. El otro responde que no. El detective solicita una repetición en cámara lenta, pero nadie tiene una.","El aroma de las empanadas llega desde un puesto cercano. Una jugadora bebe agua de su botella mientras observa cómo el perro sigue corriendo con la pelota. El equipo decide hacer una pausa hasta recuperar el equipo deportivo."],"hint":"Un momento de la vida cotidiana con familia, amigos o vecinos","facts":[{"es":"El fútbol se juega normalmente con once jugadores por equipo en los partidos oficiales.","en":"In official matches, soccer is normally played with eleven players per team."},{"es":"En los partidos informales, las reglas, el número de jugadores y el tamaño de la cancha pueden adaptarse al espacio disponible.","en":"In informal games, the rules, the number of players and the size of the field can be adapted to the space available."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí una empanada durante el descanso.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí empanadas junto a la cancha de tierra.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí una empanada después de meter un gol.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché a un papá gritar instrucciones.","heat":1},{"text":"Escuché un silbato y muchas protestas.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché gritar ¡gol! junto a dos mochilas.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a un perro correr detrás de los niños.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi dos mochilas marcando la meta.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi al portero lanzarse sobre la tierra.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba una botella de agua y una gorra.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba zapatos deportivos llenos de polvo.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una pelota vieja bajo el brazo.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui cuando comenzó a llover.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui cuando un perro robó el balón.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui cuando terminó el partido del barrio.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en la calle, con los vecinos.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba sentado en la acera, mirando.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba junto a una portería hecha con mochilas.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba pasando la tarde.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba gritando '¡pásala!' sin parar.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba persiguiendo al perro que se llevó la pelota.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"la portería","en":"goal"},{"es":"el portero","en":"goalkeeper"},{"es":"el silbato","en":"whistle"},{"es":"la cancha","en":"field"},{"es":"¡pásala!","en":"pass it!"}],"nameEn":"A neighborhood soccer game"},{"id":"espanol-nochebuena-andalucia","pack":"espanol","category":"vida-diaria","emoji":"🎄","name":"Nochebuena","fullName":"La cocina de la abuela en Nochebuena, en un pueblo de Andalucía","clues":["La abuela vigila una cazuela de barro con cordero al horno mientras su nieto intenta robar un langostino de la bandeja. Ella lo descubre sin siquiera darse la vuelta. El detective sospecha que las abuelas tienen un sistema de vigilancia más avanzado que cualquier cámara.","En el salón, los primos cantan villancicos con una zambomba y una botella de cristal que alguien rasca con una cuchara. A las nueve, el abuelo pide silencio para escuchar el mensaje del Rey en la televisión. Nadie le hace caso.","Huele a cordero asado, a sopa de almendras y a turrón recién partido. Una tía llega con una bandeja de polvorones y descubre que no queda sitio en la mesa. El detective propone mover el belén, pero nadie se atreve a tocar ni una sola oveja."],"hint":"Un momento de la vida cotidiana con familia, amigos o vecinos","facts":[{"es":"En España, muchas familias celebran la cena más importante de la Navidad la noche del 24 de diciembre, y los regalos tradicionales llegan el 6 de enero con los Reyes Magos.","en":"In Spain, many families have the most important Christmas dinner on the night of December 24, and the traditional gifts arrive on January 6 with the Three Kings."},{"es":"El turrón, un dulce de almendra y miel, se fabrica en Jijona (Alicante) desde hace siglos.","en":"Turrón, a sweet made of almonds and honey, has been made in Jijona (Alicante) for centuries."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí tanto que no pude probar el postre.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí polvorones y terminé cubierto de azúcar.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí mantecados y polvorones andaluces.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché a mis primos cantar en el salón.","heat":1},{"text":"Escuché villancicos con palmas y panderetas.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché zambombas y villancicos de Navidad.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a mi abuela vigilar una olla enorme.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi una mesa llena de turrón y mantecados.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi un belén junto a una mesa de turrones.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba un regalo escondido en una bolsa.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba una caja de dulces para la familia.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una pandereta para cantar villancicos.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui cuando los niños empezaron a dormirse.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui después de cantar junto al belén.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui después de la cena del 24 de diciembre.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en casa de la familia.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba en la cocina, cerca del horno.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba junto al belén, al lado de la zambomba.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba ayudando a poner la mesa.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba robando un langostino a escondidas.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba cantando villancicos con la zambomba.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"el belén","en":"nativity scene"},{"es":"los villancicos","en":"Christmas carols"},{"es":"la abuela","en":"grandmother"},{"es":"el turrón","en":"almond nougat"},{"es":"el langostino","en":"prawn"}],"nameEn":"Grandma's kitchen on Christmas Eve, in an Andalusian village"},{"id":"espanol-islas-galapagos","pack":"espanol","category":"naturaleza","emoji":"🐢","name":"Galápagos","fullName":"Las Islas Galápagos junto a una playa volcánica","clues":["Una iguana marina descansa sobre una roca negra mientras un lobo marino duerme cerca del sendero. Un visitante intenta pasar sin molestarlo, pero el animal ocupa todo el camino. El detective sospecha que aquí los animales tienen prioridad.","Las olas golpean las rocas y un ave marina silba desde la costa. Tiene las patas de un azul tan brillante que parecen pintadas. Una guía pide al grupo que mantenga la distancia. Un turista quiere preguntar si las patas son de verdad, pero una ráfaga de viento se lleva sus palabras y casi también su sombrero.","El aire salado se mezcla con el olor de las algas sobre las piedras calientes. Una viajera abre su mochila para sacar agua y una barra de cereal. El sol le quema los hombros, así que decide regresar al barco antes de terminar su merienda."],"hint":"Un lugar donde la naturaleza sorprende a quienes se atreven a explorar","facts":[{"es":"Las Islas Galápagos se encuentran a unos 1.000 kilómetros de la costa continental de Ecuador.","en":"The Galápagos Islands lie about 1,000 kilometers off the mainland coast of Ecuador."},{"es":"Charles Darwin visitó las islas en 1835, y sus observaciones contribuyeron al desarrollo de sus ideas sobre la evolución.","en":"Charles Darwin visited the islands in 1835, and his observations helped shape his ideas about evolution."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí fruta cerca del agua.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí una barra de cereal después de nadar.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí mientras un lobo marino dormía cerca.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché olas contra las rocas.","heat":1},{"text":"Oí aves gritar junto a la costa.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché a un ave de patas azul brillante.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a una guía explicar las reglas.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi a un turista esquivar un animal dormido.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi a una guía proteger a una iguana marina.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba una botella de agua.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba zapatos para caminar sobre lava.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba binoculares para ver aves de patas azules.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui porque hacía mucho calor.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui antes de que saliera el barco.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui porque un lobo marino bloqueaba el paso.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en una isla.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba en un sendero sobre rocas negras.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba en una playa junto a un lobo marino dormido.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba mirando animales.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba caminando con cuidado para no molestar.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba fotografiando una iguana marina.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"el lobo marino","en":"sea lion"},{"es":"la iguana marina","en":"marine iguana"},{"es":"el sendero","en":"trail"},{"es":"las olas","en":"waves"},{"es":"la roca","en":"rock"}],"nameEn":"The Galápagos Islands by a volcanic beach"},{"id":"espanol-salar-uyuni","pack":"espanol","category":"naturaleza","emoji":"🪞","name":"Salar de Uyuni","fullName":"El Salar de Uyuni después de la lluvia","clues":["Una capa delgada de agua refleja el cielo sobre una superficie blanca que parece no terminar nunca. Un turista intenta fotografiar a su amiga saltando entre las nubes reflejadas. Ella aterriza en un charco y descubre que sus zapatos no son tan impermeables como prometía la caja.","Las botas crujen sobre los cristales secos cerca del vehículo. Un guía llama al grupo para regresar antes de que cambie el tiempo. Un visitante sigue buscando el horizonte, pero el detective sospecha que el horizonte se ha escondido.","El aire frío y seco entra por la nariz mientras una viajera abre un termo de té caliente y una bolsa de galletas. La luz reflejada le obliga a ponerse lentes oscuros. Después de diez minutos, decide que sus ojos necesitan vacaciones de las vacaciones."],"hint":"Un lugar donde la naturaleza sorprende a quienes se atreven a explorar","facts":[{"es":"El Salar de Uyuni es el salar más grande del mundo y ocupa aproximadamente 10.500 kilómetros cuadrados.","en":"The Salar de Uyuni is the largest salt flat in the world, covering about 10,500 square kilometers."},{"es":"Durante la temporada de lluvias, una capa de agua puede convertir su superficie en un enorme reflejo del cielo.","en":"During the rainy season, a layer of water can turn its surface into a giant mirror of the sky."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí galletas durante la excursión.","heat":1},{"text":"Tomé un té caliente para entrar en calor.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí mientras el cielo se reflejaba bajo mis pies.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché el viento junto al vehículo.","heat":1},{"text":"Oí mis botas crujir sobre el suelo blanco.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché cristales de sal romperse bajo mis botas.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a un guía preparar una fotografía.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi a una turista saltar sobre un reflejo.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi a un guía usar figuras para fotos de perspectiva.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba lentes oscuros y agua.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba botas para caminar sobre el agua.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba lentes contra el brillo de la sal.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui porque tenía mucho frío.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui porque la luz me cansó los ojos.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui cuando el cielo y el suelo parecían uno.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en un lugar muy abierto.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba en una llanura completamente blanca.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba sobre el salar, que reflejaba el cielo.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba tomando fotos.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba haciendo fotos con perspectiva divertida.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba saltando sobre un espejo de agua y sal.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"el salar","en":"salt flat"},{"es":"la sal","en":"salt"},{"es":"el reflejo","en":"reflection"},{"es":"el cielo","en":"sky"},{"es":"los lentes oscuros","en":"sunglasses"}],"nameEn":"The Uyuni Salt Flat after the rain"},{"id":"espanol-selva-costa-rica","pack":"espanol","category":"naturaleza","emoji":"🦥","name":"Selva de Costa Rica","fullName":"Una caminata por la selva de Costa Rica","clues":["Un perezoso cuelga de una rama mientras una fila de hormigas cortadoras de hojas cruza el sendero. Un visitante se agacha para tomar una foto y descubre que sus lentes se han empañado otra vez. El detective sospecha que la humedad está trabajando para el enemigo.","Un mono aullador lanza un grito tan fuerte que un turista casi deja caer sus binoculares. La guía sonríe y señala las copas de los árboles. El detective anota que el sospechoso pesa mucho menos de lo que su voz hace pensar.","La tierra mojada y las hojas verdes llenan el aire. Una viajera abre una bolsa con gallo pinto para comer durante el descanso, pero empieza a llover. Guarda la comida, se pone el impermeable y descubre que sus calcetines ya estaban mojados."],"hint":"Un lugar donde la naturaleza sorprende a quienes se atreven a explorar","facts":[{"es":"Costa Rica alberga más de 900 especies de aves registradas.","en":"Costa Rica is home to more than 900 recorded bird species."},{"es":"Los monos aulladores producen llamadas que pueden escucharse a varios kilómetros de distancia.","en":"Howler monkeys make calls that can be heard several kilometers away."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí arroz durante un descanso.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí gallo pinto antes de caminar.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí gallo pinto antes de buscar perezosos.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché animales entre los árboles.","heat":1},{"text":"Oí un grito muy fuerte sobre mi cabeza.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché a un mono aullador desde las ramas.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a una guía señalar un árbol.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi a un turista limpiar sus lentes mojados.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi a una guía seguir hormigas cortadoras.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba una mochila y agua.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba binoculares y un impermeable.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba lentes para buscar monos y perezosos.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui porque empezó a llover.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui porque mis calcetines no se secaban.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui después de oír otro mono aullador.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en un sendero.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba bajo árboles altísimos y húmedos.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba debajo de un perezoso colgado de una rama.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba caminando con calma.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba espantando mosquitos sin éxito.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba siguiendo una fila de hormigas cortadoras.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"la selva","en":"rainforest"},{"es":"el perezoso","en":"sloth"},{"es":"el mono aullador","en":"howler monkey"},{"es":"las hormigas","en":"ants"},{"es":"el impermeable","en":"raincoat"}],"nameEn":"A hike through the Costa Rican rainforest"},{"id":"espanol-patagonia-viento","pack":"espanol","category":"naturaleza","emoji":"🏔️","name":"Patagonia","fullName":"Un sendero de la Patagonia con viento fuerte","clues":["Un excursionista intenta sujetar su gorro mientras camina frente a montañas de roca y hielo. Una ráfaga se lo arranca de la cabeza y lo manda cuesta abajo. El detective observa la persecución y decide que ningún sombrero merece tanto esfuerzo.","El viento golpea la capucha de una chaqueta y casi tapa las palabras del guía. Un cóndor pasa sobre el valle mientras alguien pregunta cuánto falta. La respuesta llega en tres partes, separadas por ráfagas.","El aire frío trae olor a tierra húmeda y vegetación baja. Una caminante intenta comer un sándwich de queso, pero el papel comienza a volar. Guarda el almuerzo, ajusta los bastones y propone regresar antes de perder también la mochila."],"hint":"Un lugar donde la naturaleza sorprende a quienes se atreven a explorar","facts":[{"es":"La Patagonia se extiende por el sur de Argentina y Chile.","en":"Patagonia stretches across southern Argentina and Chile."},{"es":"Los fuertes vientos de la región están relacionados con los vientos del oeste que circulan por las latitudes medias del hemisferio sur.","en":"The region's strong winds are linked to the westerly winds that circle the middle latitudes of the Southern Hemisphere."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí un sándwich durante la caminata.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí chocolate para recuperar energía.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí mientras el viento movía mi mochila.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché el viento contra mi chaqueta.","heat":1},{"text":"Oí ráfagas que tapaban la voz del guía.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché el viento rugir entre montañas y hielo.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a un excursionista con bastones.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi a una turista perseguir su gorro.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi a un guía señalar un cóndor sobre el valle.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba guantes y una chaqueta.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba bastones y un gorro bien ajustado.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una correa para que no volara mi gorro.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui porque tenía las manos frías.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui cuando casi perdí mi sombrero.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui antes de que el viento robara mi mochila.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba al aire libre.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba en un sendero entre montañas.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba frente a un glaciar, luchando contra el viento.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba caminando bastante.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba sujetando mi gorro con las dos manos.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba persiguiendo mi gorro cuesta abajo.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"el viento","en":"wind"},{"es":"la ráfaga","en":"gust"},{"es":"el gorro","en":"hat, beanie"},{"es":"el glaciar","en":"glacier"},{"es":"cuesta abajo","en":"downhill"}],"nameEn":"A windy trail in Patagonia"},{"id":"espanol-cataratas-iguazu","pack":"espanol","category":"naturaleza","emoji":"💦","name":"Cataratas del Iguazú","fullName":"Las cataratas del Iguazú desde una pasarela","clues":["Una enorme cortina de agua cae frente a una pasarela metálica. Un visitante levanta su teléfono para tomar una foto, pero una nube de gotas cubre la pantalla. El detective sospecha que el paisaje no quiere dejar pruebas.","El rugido del agua es tan fuerte que una guía debe señalar el camino con las manos. Un turista intenta hacer una pregunta y solo recibe una sonrisa. El detective recomienda escribir mensajes, aunque el papel tampoco duraría mucho.","El aire huele a vegetación mojada y agua fresca. Una familia guarda sus chipás en una mochila para protegerlos de las gotas. Un niño descubre que tiene los calcetines empapados y anuncia que ya está listo para regresar al hotel."],"hint":"Un lugar donde la naturaleza sorprende a quienes se atreven a explorar","facts":[{"es":"Las cataratas del Iguazú se encuentran en la frontera entre Argentina y Brasil.","en":"The Iguazú Falls are on the border between Argentina and Brazil."},{"es":"El sistema tiene aproximadamente 275 saltos de agua, aunque el número visible puede cambiar según el nivel del río.","en":"The system has about 275 waterfalls, although the number you can see changes with the river level."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí algo rápido durante la visita.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí chipá cerca de una pasarela.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí chipá mientras el agua rugía cerca.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché agua caer con mucha fuerza.","heat":1},{"text":"Oí un ruido que tapaba todas las voces.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché el rugido de la Garganta del Diablo.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a una guía señalar el camino.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi a un turista proteger su cámara del agua.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi a una guía empapada junto a la pasarela.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba una botella y mi teléfono.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba una funda impermeable para la cámara.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una capa contra el agua de los saltos.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui porque estaba empapado.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui porque no podía escuchar a mi familia.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui después de ver la Garganta del Diablo.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en un parque natural.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba en una pasarela metálica.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba frente a la Garganta del Diablo.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba mirando el paisaje.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba secando la pantalla de mi teléfono.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba empapado por la nube de agua de la cascada.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"las cataratas","en":"waterfalls"},{"es":"la pasarela","en":"walkway"},{"es":"empapado","en":"soaked"},{"es":"el rugido","en":"roar"},{"es":"las gotas","en":"drops"}],"nameEn":"Iguazú Falls from a walkway"},{"id":"espanol-chichen-itza-equinoccio","pack":"espanol","category":"historia-y-cultura","emoji":"🐍","name":"Chichén Itzá","fullName":"Chichén Itzá cerca del equinoccio","clues":["La luz del sol forma una serie de triángulos de sombra sobre la gran escalinata de piedra. Un guía señala la figura que parece bajar por el costado del edificio. Un visitante intenta fotografiarla, pero descubre que su sombrero ocupa la mitad de la imagen.","Un grupo escucha la explicación de una guía mientras los pájaros cantan entre los árboles. Un turista aplaude frente a la estructura y escucha un eco extraño. El detective anota que hasta las paredes parecen tener algo que responder.","El calor levanta el olor de la tierra seca y la vegetación. Una familia comparte agua y pequeños paquetes de galletas bajo la sombra de un árbol. Una niña se abanica con un folleto y propone salir antes de que el sol gane la discusión."],"hint":"Un lugar donde el pasado y las tradiciones siguen presentes","facts":[{"es":"Chichén Itzá fue una importante ciudad de la civilización maya en la península de Yucatán.","en":"Chichén Itzá was an important city of the Maya civilization on the Yucatán Peninsula."},{"es":"Cerca de los equinoccios, la luz y la sombra pueden crear una figura que parece una serpiente descendiendo por la escalinata de El Castillo.","en":"Around the equinoxes, light and shadow can create a figure that looks like a serpent descending the staircase of El Castillo."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí galletas bajo un árbol.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí después de caminar entre piedras antiguas.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí mientras esperaba la serpiente de luz.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché a una guía contar historias.","heat":1},{"text":"Oí un eco extraño después de un aplauso.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché aplausos frente a la gran escalinata.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a una guía señalar una pared.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi a turistas esperar una sombra especial.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi a una guía explicar la serpiente de luz.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba agua y un sombrero.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba un folleto sobre una ciudad antigua.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una foto de la escalinata de Kukulkán.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui porque el sol calentaba mucho.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui después de observar las sombras.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui cuando desapareció la serpiente de luz.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en un sitio arqueológico.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba en una explanada con mucha gente.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba frente a la escalinata de El Castillo.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba escuchando a un guía.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba esperando a que bajara el sol.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba viendo bajar la sombra de la serpiente.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"la escalinata","en":"grand staircase"},{"es":"la sombra","en":"shadow"},{"es":"la serpiente","en":"serpent"},{"es":"el eco","en":"echo"},{"es":"el sitio arqueológico","en":"archaeological site"}],"nameEn":"Chichén Itzá near the equinox"},{"id":"espanol-alhambra-granada","pack":"espanol","category":"historia-y-cultura","emoji":"🦁","name":"La Alhambra","fullName":"Los patios de la Alhambra en Granada","clues":["Un visitante observa los delicados diseños geométricos de una pared mientras una guía explica cómo se repiten las figuras. En el centro del patio, una fuente sostenida por leones de piedra atrae todas las cámaras. El detective sospecha que los animales llevan siglos posando sin cobrar.","El agua corre suavemente por los canales del patio. Un niño intenta contar los leones de la fuente, pero pierde la cuenta cuando otro visitante pasa frente a él. Su madre propone empezar de nuevo. El niño solicita una calculadora.","El aroma de los jardines y las plantas cercanas se mezcla con el aire fresco de la mañana. Una viajera guarda una bolsa con un bocadillo y una botella de agua. Después de caminar por varios patios, decide buscar una banca antes de continuar."],"hint":"Un lugar donde el pasado y las tradiciones siguen presentes","facts":[{"es":"La Alhambra fue ampliada principalmente durante el gobierno de la dinastía nazarí en los siglos XIII y XIV.","en":"The Alhambra was expanded mainly under the Nasrid dynasty in the 13th and 14th centuries."},{"es":"La famosa Fuente de los Leones está sostenida por doce esculturas de leones.","en":"The famous Fountain of the Lions rests on twelve lion sculptures."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí un bocadillo después de caminar.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí cerca de unos jardines antiguos.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí después de ver la Fuente de los Leones.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché agua correr en un patio.","heat":1},{"text":"Oí una fuente entre paredes decoradas.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché agua junto a doce leones de piedra.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a una guía explicar unos dibujos.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi a un niño contar animales de piedra.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi a una guía explicar los palacios nazaríes.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba una botella de agua.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba un plano de patios y jardines.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una foto del Patio de los Leones.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui porque me dolían los pies.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui después de visitar varios patios.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui después de contar los doce leones.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en un edificio antiguo.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba en un patio con una fuente.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba en el Patio de los Leones.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba haciendo una visita guiada.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba mirando dibujos geométricos en la pared.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba contando los leones de la fuente.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"el patio","en":"courtyard"},{"es":"la fuente","en":"fountain"},{"es":"los leones","en":"lions"},{"es":"los jardines","en":"gardens"},{"es":"la piedra","en":"stone"}],"nameEn":"The courtyards of the Alhambra in Granada"},{"id":"espanol-dia-muertos-ofrenda","pack":"espanol","category":"historia-y-cultura","emoji":"🕯️","name":"Día de Muertos","fullName":"Una ofrenda familiar del Día de Muertos","clues":["Una familia coloca fotografías, velas y flores anaranjadas sobre una mesa decorada. Una niña acomoda con cuidado el retrato de su abuelo. El perro se acerca al pan dulce y recibe una mirada que significa claramente que ese alimento no es para él.","Una canción favorita del abuelo suena desde una pequeña bocina mientras la familia comparte recuerdos. Un tío cuenta una historia divertida y todos sonríen. El detective comprende que algunas personas siguen presentes en las conversaciones de quienes las aman.","El aroma del copal y las flores se mezcla con el chocolate caliente y el pan recién colocado. Una madre lleva una taza a la mesa, pero el perro vuelve a acercarse. La familia decide mover el plato antes de que el visitante de cuatro patas cometa un robo."],"hint":"Un lugar donde el pasado y las tradiciones siguen presentes","facts":[{"es":"El Día de Muertos se celebra principalmente el 1 y 2 de noviembre en México.","en":"Day of the Dead is celebrated mainly on November 1 and 2 in Mexico."},{"es":"Las ofrendas pueden incluir fotografías, velas, flores y alimentos que les gustaban a las personas recordadas.","en":"Ofrendas (home altars) can include photographs, candles, flowers and foods the remembered loved ones enjoyed."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí pan dulce con mi familia.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí pan de muerto con chocolate caliente.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí pan de muerto junto a las flores naranjas.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché una canción familiar.","heat":1},{"text":"Oí historias sobre personas muy queridas.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché la canción favorita de mi abuelo.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a una niña colocar una fotografía.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi a una familia preparar una mesa especial.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi a una niña poner flores de cempasúchil.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba una fotografía antigua.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba velas y flores para recordar a alguien.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una foto para colocar en la ofrenda.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui después de estar con mi familia.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui cuando terminamos de decorar la mesa.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui después de recordar a mis seres queridos.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en casa con la familia.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba junto a una mesa llena de velas.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba frente a la ofrenda, entre cempasúchil.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba recordando a alguien querido.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba encendiendo velas con cuidado.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba poniendo pan de muerto en la ofrenda.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"la ofrenda","en":"home altar"},{"es":"las velas","en":"candles"},{"es":"el cempasúchil","en":"marigold"},{"es":"el pan de muerto","en":"bread of the dead"},{"es":"los seres queridos","en":"loved ones"}],"nameEn":"A family Day of the Dead altar"},{"id":"espanol-camino-santiago","pack":"espanol","category":"historia-y-cultura","emoji":"🐚","name":"Camino de Santiago","fullName":"El Camino de Santiago al llegar a Galicia","clues":["Una peregrina camina con una mochila grande y un bastón de madera. Sus botas están cubiertas de polvo y tiene una ampolla en el talón. Cuando ve una señal amarilla que indica la ruta, sonríe como si acabara de encontrar un tesoro.","Las botas golpean el sendero mientras una campana suena desde una iglesia cercana. Un caminante pregunta cuánto falta para llegar al próximo pueblo. Su compañero responde que poco, pero el detective sospecha que sus definiciones de distancia son diferentes.","El aroma del pan recién hecho llega desde una cafetería. Dos viajeros comparten una tortilla de patatas y llenan sus botellas de agua. Una peregrina decide quedarse un rato más porque sus pies han presentado una protesta formal."],"hint":"Un lugar donde el pasado y las tradiciones siguen presentes","facts":[{"es":"El Camino de Santiago es una red de rutas de peregrinación que llevan a Santiago de Compostela.","en":"The Camino de Santiago is a network of pilgrimage routes that lead to Santiago de Compostela."},{"es":"La tradición de peregrinar a Santiago de Compostela tiene más de mil años de historia.","en":"The tradition of walking to Santiago de Compostela is more than a thousand years old."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí un bocadillo durante el descanso.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí tortilla de patatas en un pueblo.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí después de seguir las flechas amarillas.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché campanas desde una iglesia.","heat":1},{"text":"Oí bastones golpear el camino de piedra.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché campanas al acercarme a la catedral.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a una viajera con una mochila enorme.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi a un caminante curarse una ampolla.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi a un peregrino seguir flechas amarillas.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba una mochila y una botella.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba un bastón y un mapa de la ruta.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una credencial llena de sellos.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui porque tenía los pies cansados.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui después de descansar en un albergue.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui cuando mis ampollas pidieron descanso.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en un camino rural.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba en un albergue lleno de botas.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba junto a un mojón con una concha amarilla.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba caminando mucho.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba curándome una ampolla en el talón.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba sellando mi credencial de peregrino.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"el peregrino","en":"pilgrim"},{"es":"la ampolla","en":"blister"},{"es":"el bastón","en":"walking stick"},{"es":"el albergue","en":"hostel"},{"es":"la concha","en":"shell"}],"nameEn":"The Camino de Santiago arriving in Galicia"},{"id":"espanol-rapa-nui-moai","pack":"espanol","category":"historia-y-cultura","emoji":"🗿","name":"Rapa Nui","fullName":"Los moái de Rapa Nui (Isla de Pascua)","clues":["Una fila de enormes figuras de piedra mira hacia el interior de la isla, de espaldas al mar. Un turista intenta copiar su expresión seria para una foto, pero se ríe a los tres segundos. El detective concluye que las figuras llevan siglos de práctica.","El viento del Pacífico silba sobre la hierba mientras unos caballos sueltos pasan cerca del camino. Una guía rapanui explica que está prohibido tocar las figuras o subirse a las plataformas. Un niño baja la mano justo a tiempo.","Huele a mar, a hierba mojada y a las empanadas de atún que una familia trajo para el almuerzo. Una viajera mira la hora y propone volver al hotel, pero cambia de idea cuando el cielo empieza a ponerse naranja detrás de los gigantes de piedra."],"hint":"Un lugar donde el pasado y las tradiciones siguen presentes","facts":[{"es":"Rapa Nui está en el océano Pacífico, a más de 3.500 kilómetros de la costa de Chile continental.","en":"Rapa Nui sits in the Pacific Ocean, more than 3,500 kilometers from mainland Chile."},{"es":"En la isla hay casi mil moái, tallados en su mayoría en la roca volcánica de la cantera de Rano Raraku.","en":"The island has almost a thousand moai, most of them carved from the volcanic rock of the Rano Raraku quarry."}],"cards":{"food":[{"text":"Comí pescado después de caminar.","heat":1},{"text":"Comí un curanto preparado con piedras calientes.","heat":2},{"text":"Comí curanto después de ver figuras gigantes.","heat":3}],"sound":[{"text":"Escuché olas y viento cerca de la costa.","heat":1},{"text":"Oí el viento pasar entre figuras de piedra.","heat":2},{"text":"Escuché olas junto a las figuras de Ahu Tongariki.","heat":3}],"people":[{"text":"Vi a una guía explicar una tradición.","heat":1},{"text":"Vi a un visitante mirar enormes rostros de piedra.","heat":2},{"text":"Vi a una guía explicar los quince moáis.","heat":3}],"object":[{"text":"Llevaba agua y una cámara.","heat":1},{"text":"Llevaba un sombrero contra el viento del Pacífico.","heat":2},{"text":"Llevaba una foto de quince figuras sobre un ahu.","heat":3}],"leaving":[{"text":"Me fui porque el viento era muy fuerte.","heat":1},{"text":"Me fui después de ver las figuras al amanecer.","heat":2},{"text":"Me fui cuando el sol iluminó los quince moáis.","heat":3}],"where":[{"text":"Estaba en una isla lejana.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba en una colina con mucho pasto.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba frente a una fila de moái.","heat":3}],"doing":[{"text":"Estaba haciendo turismo.","heat":1},{"text":"Estaba esquivando caballos salvajes.","heat":2},{"text":"Estaba imitando la cara seria de un moái.","heat":3}]},"vocab":[{"es":"la isla","en":"island"},{"es":"las figuras de piedra","en":"stone figures"},{"es":"los caballos","en":"horses"},{"es":"la costa","en":"coast"},{"es":"el amanecer","en":"sunrise"}],"nameEn":"The moai of Rapa Nui (Easter Island)"}],"comedy":{"inspector":{"caseStartDetective":[{"en":"You were there. Act natural. You're terrible at acting natural.","es":"Tú estuviste ahí. Actúa normal. Eres pésimo actuando normal."},{"en":"Memorize the scene. I'll know if you're winging it. I always know.","es":"Memoriza la escena. Si improvisas, lo sabré. Siempre lo sé."},{"en":"One of these fine citizens is lying. Statistically, the one sweating. Unfortunately, everyone's sweating.","es":"Uno de estos ciudadanos miente. Estadísticamente, el que suda. Por desgracia, todos sudan."}],"caseStartLiar":[{"en":"You weren't there. Lie like your Wi-Fi depends on it.","es":"No estuviste ahí. Miente como si tu wifi dependiera de ello."},{"en":"Blend in. Nod a lot. Never say 'I was definitely there.'","es":"Mézclate. Asiente mucho. Nunca digas 'yo definitivamente estuve ahí'."},{"en":"All you've got is a hint and confidence. Mostly confidence.","es":"Solo tienes una pista y confianza. Sobre todo confianza."}],"questionAsked":[{"en":"Answer carefully. I've had four coffees and zero patience.","es":"Responde con cuidado. Llevo cuatro cafés y cero paciencia."},{"en":"Prove you were there. Without drawing the Liar a map.","es":"Demuestra que estuviste ahí. Sin dibujarle un mapa al mentiroso."},{"en":"Take your time. Actually, don't. I'm watching the clock.","es":"Tómate tu tiempo. Bueno, no. Estoy mirando el reloj."}],"revealAllMatch":[{"en":"Four perfect stories. I've never been more suspicious in my life.","es":"Cuatro historias perfectas. Nunca había sospechado tanto en mi vida."},{"en":"Everyone agrees. That's exactly what liars do.","es":"Todos coinciden. Justo lo que hacen los mentirosos."},{"en":"Smooth. Too smooth. Somebody here rehearsed.","es":"Muy limpio. Demasiado limpio. Alguien aquí ensayó."}],"revealDecoy":[{"en":"Hmm. Not everyone was at the same place…","es":"Mmm. No todos estuvieron en el mismo lugar…"},{"en":"One of these stories just tripped over its own shoelaces.","es":"Una de estas historias acaba de tropezar con sus propios cordones."},{"en":"*spits coffee* …Somebody's been to a different party.","es":"*escupe el café* …Alguien estuvo en otra fiesta."}],"revealHot":[{"en":"Subtle as a marching band.","es":"Discreto como una banda de música."},{"en":"Why not just send the Liar a postcard?","es":"¿Por qué no le mandas una postal al mentiroso?"},{"en":"Bold. Honest. Possibly disastrous.","es":"Valiente. Honesto. Posiblemente desastroso."}],"revealDuplicate":[{"en":"Two of you gave the SAME answer. Coordinated? Or just boring?","es":"Dos dieron la MISMA respuesta. ¿Coordinados? ¿O solo aburridos?"},{"en":"Copy-paste alibis. My favorite kind of evidence.","es":"Coartadas de copiar y pegar. Mi tipo de prueba favorita."}],"voteStart":[{"en":"Point a finger. Ruin a friendship. Standard procedure.","es":"Señala a alguien. Arruina una amistad. Procedimiento estándar."},{"en":"Somebody's lying. Pick wisely. Or dramatically.","es":"Alguien miente. Elige con sabiduría. O con drama."},{"en":"Trust your gut. My gut says nachos, but that's unrelated.","es":"Confía en tu instinto. El mío dice nachos, pero no tiene que ver."}],"liarCaught":[{"en":"Case closed. Somebody get this person a worse lawyer.","es":"Caso cerrado. Que alguien le consiga un abogado peor."},{"en":"Gotcha. That alibi had more holes than my socks.","es":"Te atrapé. Esa coartada tenía más agujeros que mis calcetines."},{"en":"Justice is served. With a side of embarrassment.","es":"Se hizo justicia. Con guarnición de vergüenza."}],"liarEscaped":[{"en":"They got away. I'm retiring. Again.","es":"Se escapó. Me retiro. Otra vez."},{"en":"Fooled by an amateur. Nobody tell my mother.","es":"Me engañó un aficionado. Que nadie se lo cuente a mi madre."},{"en":"*stares into coffee* …I used to be good at this.","es":"*mira su café* …Antes era bueno en esto."}],"tie":[{"en":"A tie. Democracy has failed us. The Liar walks.","es":"Empate. La democracia nos falló. El mentiroso se va."},{"en":"Three suspects, three votes, zero brains. Liar escapes.","es":"Tres sospechosos, tres votos, cero cerebros. El mentiroso escapa."}],"liarGuessRight":[{"en":"They guessed the place?! Who taught them that? …Was it me?","es":"¿¡Adivinó el lugar!? ¿Quién le enseñó eso? …¿Fui yo?"},{"en":"Caught, but clever. I hate it. I respect it.","es":"Atrapado, pero listo. Lo odio. Lo respeto."}],"liarGuessWrong":[{"en":"Wrong. So, so wrong. Take them away.","es":"Error. Un error enorme. Llévenselo."},{"en":"Not even close. I've seen better guesses from a parrot.","es":"Ni cerca. He visto mejores intentos de un loro."}],"gameEnd":[{"en":"Same time tomorrow? Bring better alibis.","es":"¿Mañana a la misma hora? Traigan mejores coartadas."},{"en":"Nobody leaves until we play again. That's the law. I just made it up.","es":"Nadie se va hasta jugar otra vez. Es la ley. Me la acabo de inventar."}]},"suspects":{"chef-bruno":{"onReveal":[{"en":"The food there? A crime. But not MY crime.","es":"¿La comida de ahí? Un crimen. Pero no MI crimen."},{"en":"I only remember the snacks. As one does.","es":"Solo recuerdo los bocadillos. Como debe ser."},{"en":"I would never lie. I might over-season.","es":"Yo nunca mentiría. Quizás pondría demasiada sal."}],"onVoted":[{"en":"Me?! I have flour on my hands, not guilt!","es":"¡¿Yo?! ¡Tengo harina en las manos, no culpa!"},{"en":"You'll regret this at dinnertime.","es":"Te arrepentirás a la hora de cenar."}]},"skater-leo":{"onReveal":[{"en":"Whatever. I was there. Probably.","es":"Da igual. Estuve ahí. Probablemente."},{"en":"It was mid. Honestly.","es":"Estuvo regular. La verdad."},{"en":"Can we skip to the part where I win?","es":"¿Podemos saltar a la parte donde gano?"}],"onVoted":[{"en":"Wow. Okay. Cool. Cool cool cool.","es":"Guau. Vale. Genial. Genial genial genial."},{"en":"I'm telling everyone you did this.","es":"Le voy a contar a todos que hiciste esto."}]},"rosa":{"onReveal":[{"en":"I didn't do it! …What are we talking about?","es":"¡Yo no fui! …¿De qué estamos hablando?"},{"en":"*sweating intensifies*","es":"*suda todavía más*"},{"en":"I always look guilty. It's a medical mystery.","es":"Siempre parezco culpable. Es un misterio médico."}],"onVoted":[{"en":"It's the sweat, isn't it? IT'S ALWAYS THE SWEAT.","es":"Es por el sudor, ¿verdad? SIEMPRE ES EL SUDOR."},{"en":"Et tu?! I shared my snacks with you!","es":"¡¿Tú también?! ¡Compartí mis bocadillos contigo!"}]},"mr-sterling":{"onReveal":[{"en":"*adjusts cufflinks* Naturally, I was there.","es":"*se acomoda los gemelos* Naturalmente, estuve ahí."},{"en":"I attend all events. Usually by invitation.","es":"Asisto a todos los eventos. Normalmente con invitación."},{"en":"My alibi is impeccable. Like my suit.","es":"Mi coartada es impecable. Como mi traje."}],"onVoted":[{"en":"How… pedestrian of you.","es":"Qué… vulgar de tu parte."},{"en":"My lawyer will hear about this. All four of them.","es":"Mi abogado se enterará. Los cuatro."}]},"sunny":{"onReveal":[{"en":"Wait, let me take a photo of my alibi.","es":"Espera, déjame tomarle una foto a mi coartada."},{"en":"Best trip ever! Where was I again?","es":"¡El mejor viaje! ¿Dónde estaba yo?"},{"en":"I have 400 photos as proof. None in focus.","es":"Tengo 400 fotos de prueba. Ninguna enfocada."}],"onVoted":[{"en":"This is going in my travel blog. Badly.","es":"Esto va a mi blog de viajes. Muy mal."},{"en":"Rude. I brought you a souvenir.","es":"Qué grosero. Te traje un recuerdo."}]},"granny-dot":{"name":"Granny Dot","bio":{"en":"87. Knits. Has outlived four detectives.","es":"87 años. Teje. Ha sobrevivido a cuatro detectives."},"onReveal":[{"en":"I'm 87, sweetie. I was everywhere.","es":"Tengo 87 años, cariño. Estuve en todas partes."},{"en":"*knits aggressively*","es":"*teje con mucha agresividad*"},{"en":"In my day, we lied with dignity.","es":"En mis tiempos, mentíamos con dignidad."},{"en":"I brought cookies. That's my alibi.","es":"Traje galletas. Esa es mi coartada."}],"onVoted":[{"en":"I've outlived four detectives. I'll outlive you.","es":"He enterrado a cuatro detectives. Te enterraré a ti."},{"en":"No more cookies for you. Ever.","es":"No hay más galletas para ti. Nunca."},{"en":"I'm calling your mother.","es":"Voy a llamar a tu madre."}]},"big-tony":{"name":"Big Tony","bio":{"en":"Looks like a mob boss. Is a kindergarten teacher.","es":"Parece un capo de la mafia. Es maestro de kínder."},"onReveal":[{"en":"*sips juice box menacingly*","es":"*sorbe su jugo de cajita de forma amenazante*"},{"en":"I was there. Ask my kindergarten class.","es":"Estuve ahí. Pregúntale a mi grupo de kínder."},{"en":"Nobody leaves until everyone washes their hands.","es":"Nadie se va hasta que todos se laven las manos."},{"en":"I know a guy. He's six. He'll vouch for me.","es":"Conozco a alguien. Tiene seis años. Responderá por mí."}],"onVoted":[{"en":"That's a timeout. For you.","es":"Eso es un tiempo fuera. Para ti."},{"en":"I'm not mad. I'm disappointed.","es":"No estoy enojado. Estoy decepcionado."},{"en":"Use your words. Not your finger.","es":"Usa tus palabras. No tu dedo."}]}},"objection":{"banner":{"en":"OBJECTION!","es":"¡PROTESTO!"},"prompt":{"en":"You've been accused! Pick your excuse — fast!","es":"¡Te acusaron! Elige tu excusa, ¡rápido!"},"excuses":[{"en":"I have an identical twin. SHE'S the liar.","es":"Tengo una gemela idéntica. ELLA es la mentirosa."},{"en":"That was a metaphor.","es":"Eso fue una metáfora."},{"en":"I was undercover. As a lamp.","es":"Estaba de incógnito. Como lámpara."},{"en":"Autocorrect did that.","es":"Eso fue el autocorrector."},{"en":"I was there in spirit. Very much in spirit.","es":"Estuve ahí en espíritu. Muchísimo en espíritu."},{"en":"My memory is fine. My memory is fine. My memory is…","es":"Mi memoria está bien. Mi memoria está bien. Mi memoria…"},{"en":"Ask my mom. She'll say I'm a good kid.","es":"Pregúntale a mi mamá. Te dirá que soy buena persona."},{"en":"I don't remember, therefore it didn't happen.","es":"No me acuerdo, por lo tanto no pasó."},{"en":"In my defense, I was hungry.","es":"En mi defensa, tenía hambre."},{"en":"I plead the snack.","es":"Me acojo al derecho del bocadillo."},{"en":"That's what the REAL liar would say.","es":"Eso es lo que diría el VERDADERO mentiroso."},{"en":"I was facing the other way. The entire time.","es":"Estaba mirando hacia el otro lado. Todo el tiempo."},{"en":"I'm not lying. I'm creatively remembering.","es":"No miento. Recuerdo de forma creativa."},{"en":"I blinked. A lot happened.","es":"Parpadeé. Pasaron muchas cosas."},{"en":"My GPS was on airplane mode.","es":"Mi GPS estaba en modo avión."},{"en":"Objection to your objection.","es":"Protesto contra tu protesta."},{"en":"I'm too good-looking to lie.","es":"Soy demasiado guapo para mentir."},{"en":"I was there. Spiritually, emotionally, almost physically.","es":"Estuve ahí. Espiritual, emocional y casi físicamente."},{"en":"That card slipped. My finger has a mind of its own.","es":"Se me resbaló la carta. Mi dedo tiene vida propia."},{"en":"I was distracted by a very interesting pigeon.","es":"Me distrajo una paloma muy interesante."},{"en":"Check the security cameras! …Actually, don't.","es":"¡Revisen las cámaras! …Mejor no."},{"en":"I'm allergic to lying. Medically.","es":"Soy alérgico a mentir. Médicamente."},{"en":"Everyone remembers things differently. Some of us incorrectly.","es":"Cada uno recuerda distinto. Algunos, mal."},{"en":"I have no further comments. *sweats*","es":"No tengo más comentarios. *suda*"}],"inspectorAfter":[{"en":"The court accepts that excuse. The court does NOT believe it.","es":"El tribunal acepta la excusa. El tribunal NO se la cree."},{"en":"Noted. Laughed at. Noted again.","es":"Anotado. Me reí. Anotado otra vez."},{"en":"That's the worst excuse I've heard today. And it's been a long day.","es":"Es la peor excusa que he oído hoy. Y ha sido un día largo."}]},"mugshot":{"title":{"en":"CAUGHT","es":"ATRAPADO"},"chargeTemplate":{"en":"CHARGED WITH: saying \"{answer}\"… at a {place}.","es":"ACUSADO DE: decir \"{answer}\"… en {place}."},"chargeFallback":[{"en":"CHARGED WITH: being suspiciously vague in public.","es":"ACUSADO DE: ser sospechosamente vago en público."},{"en":"CHARGED WITH: first-degree bluffing.","es":"ACUSADO DE: farolear en primer grado."},{"en":"CHARGED WITH: lying with a straight face. Almost.","es":"ACUSADO DE: mentir con cara seria. Casi."}],"escapedTitle":{"en":"STILL AT LARGE","es":"SIGUE PRÓFUGO"},"escapedLine":[{"en":"Wanted for: fooling the entire room.","es":"Buscado por: engañar a todo el grupo."},{"en":"Last seen: blending in suspiciously well.","es":"Visto por última vez: mezclándose sospechosamente bien."}]},"awards":[{"id":"smooth-criminal","en":"🕴️ Smooth Criminal — escaped as the Liar","es":"🕴️ Criminal Elegante — escapó como mentiroso"},{"id":"master-detective","en":"🔎 Master Detective — most correct votes","es":"🔎 Detective Maestro — más votos correctos"},{"id":"suspicious-innocent","en":"😰 Most Suspicious Innocent — most votes while innocent","es":"😰 Inocente Más Sospechoso — más votos siendo inocente"},{"id":"loudmouth","en":"📢 Loudmouth — played the most 🔥🔥🔥 cards","es":"📢 Bocazas — jugó más cartas 🔥🔥🔥"},{"id":"drama-queen","en":"🎭 Drama Queen — used Objection!","es":"🎭 Reina del Drama — usó ¡Protesto!"}]},"translations":{"Comí maíz caliente y me quemé la lengua.":"I ate hot corn and burned my tongue.","Comí esquites con limón y mucho chile.":"I ate esquites with lime and lots of chili.","Comí esquites frente a la Catedral Metropolitana.":"I ate esquites in front of the Metropolitan Cathedral.","Escuché una campana que tapó mi conversación.":"I heard a bell drown out my conversation.","Escuché las campanas de una catedral enorme.":"I heard the bells of a huge cathedral.","Escuché las campanas junto al Palacio Nacional.":"I heard the bells next to the National Palace.","Vi a un niño perseguir una burbuja gigante.":"I saw a kid chase a giant bubble.","Vi una bandera tan grande como mi edificio.":"I saw a flag as big as my building.","Vi la bandera gigante en la Plaza de la Constitución.":"I saw the giant flag in Constitution Square.","Llevaba un mapa que el viento dobló por mí.":"I had a map the wind folded for me.","Llevaba una foto del Palacio Nacional.":"I had a photo of the National Palace.","Llevaba una guía del antiguo centro mexica.":"I had a guide to the old Aztec city center.","Me fui porque mis zapatos ya pedían descanso.":"I left because my shoes were begging for rest.","Me fui cuando empezó a llover sobre la plaza.":"I left when it started raining on the square.","Me fui cuando bajaron la bandera monumental.":"I left when they lowered the giant flag.","Estaba en una plaza muy grande.":"I was in a very big square.","Estaba cerca de unos vendedores de globos.":"I was near some balloon sellers.","Estaba frente a la Catedral Metropolitana.":"I was in front of the Metropolitan Cathedral.","Estaba paseando con mi familia.":"I was walking around with my family.","Estaba persiguiendo una burbuja gigante.":"I was chasing a giant bubble.","Estaba viendo cómo bajaban la bandera enorme.":"I was watching them lower the huge flag.","El Zócalo de Ciudad de México un domingo":"Mexico City's Zócalo on a Sunday","Un niño persigue una burbuja gigante frente a la Catedral Metropolitana mientras su padre intenta tomar una foto. La burbuja explota justo cuando el padre sonríe. El detective sospecha que el niño considera esto una victoria.":"A boy chases a giant bubble in front of the Metropolitan Cathedral while his father tries to take a photo. The bubble pops just as the father smiles. The detective suspects the boy considers this a victory.","Una campana de la catedral suena sobre la plaza. Un vendedor ofrece globos de colores y una familia discute si todavía tiene tiempo para visitar el Palacio Nacional. La abuela ya decidió que primero van a comer.":"A cathedral bell rings over the square. A vendor offers colorful balloons and a family argues about whether they still have time to visit the National Palace. Grandma has already decided they're eating first.","El olor de los esquites calientes llega desde un puesto cercano. Una señora sostiene un vaso de maíz con limón y chile mientras busca una servilleta. El viento se lleva la primera que encuentra, y el detective empieza a investigar al sospechoso invisible.":"The smell of hot esquites drifts over from a nearby stand. A woman holds a cup of corn with lime and chili while looking for a napkin. The wind steals the first one she finds, and the detective starts investigating the invisible suspect.","La plaza principal de Ciudad de México se llama oficialmente Plaza de la Constitución.":"Mexico City's main square is officially called Plaza de la Constitución (Constitution Square).","La Catedral Metropolitana comenzó a construirse en 1573 y tardó más de dos siglos en completarse.":"Construction of the Metropolitan Cathedral began in 1573 and took more than two centuries to finish.","Comí algo crujiente y pedí otra porción.":"I ate something crunchy and ordered another serving.","Comí una tlayuda más grande que mi plato.":"I ate a tlayuda bigger than my plate.","Comí chapulines tostados y pedí agua.":"I ate toasted grasshoppers and asked for water.","Escuché a dos vendedores discutir un precio.":"I heard two vendors argue over a price.","Escuché tortillas caer sobre un comal caliente.":"I heard tortillas hit a hot griddle.","Escuché el comal junto a las tlayudas.":"I heard the griddle next to the tlayudas.","Vi canastas de colores hasta el techo.":"I saw colorful baskets stacked to the ceiling.","Vi montones de chiles secos y chocolate.":"I saw piles of dried chiles and chocolate.","Vi siete tipos de mole en un solo puesto.":"I saw seven kinds of mole at a single stall.","Llevaba una bolsa que terminó demasiado llena.":"I had a bag that ended up way too full.","Llevaba una bolsa de mole para mi familia.":"I had a bag of mole for my family.","Llevaba chocolate para preparar con agua caliente.":"I had chocolate to make with hot water.","Me fui porque ya no podía cargar mis compras.":"I left because I couldn't carry my shopping anymore.","Me fui cuando el humo me hizo llorar.":"I left when the smoke made me cry.","Me fui con una tlayuda que no cabía en mi bolsa.":"I left with a tlayuda that didn't fit in my bag.","Estaba en un pasillo con muchos puestos.":"I was in an aisle full of stalls.","Estaba entre bolsas de chiles secos.":"I was between bags of dried chiles.","Estaba frente a un puesto de chapulines.":"I was in front of a grasshopper stall.","Estaba comprando algo para comer.":"I was buying something to eat.","Estaba regateando por unas especias.":"I was haggling over some spices.","Estaba probando un chapulín. Uno solo.":"I was trying a grasshopper. Just one.","Un mercado tradicional en Oaxaca":"A traditional market in Oaxaca","Una vendedora coloca chapulines tostados junto a bolsas de chiles secos. Un visitante observa los insectos con mucha curiosidad, pero mantiene una distancia respetable. El detective anota que el valor cambia cuando la comida tiene patas.":"A vendor sets toasted grasshoppers next to bags of dried chiles. A visitor studies the insects with great curiosity, but keeps a respectable distance. The detective notes that courage changes when food has legs.","Una mujer pregunta el precio de una canasta mientras un cocinero golpea una tortilla contra el comal. Al fondo, alguien llama a su hijo para que deje de mirar los dulces. El niño responde que está haciendo una investigación importante.":"A woman asks the price of a basket while a cook slaps a tortilla onto the griddle. In the back, someone tells their son to stop staring at the candy. The boy replies that he's conducting an important investigation.","El aroma del chocolate caliente se mezcla con el de las tlayudas que se tuestan sobre el comal. Un cliente se termina su taza de chocolate, mira el pan que todavía tiene en la bolsa y pide otra taza. El detective comprende que algunas investigaciones requieren repetir la prueba.":"The aroma of hot chocolate mixes with tlayudas toasting on the griddle. A customer finishes his cup of chocolate, looks at the bread still in his bag, and orders another cup. The detective understands that some investigations require repeating the test.","Oaxaca es conocida por su gran variedad de tradiciones culinarias y por sus diferentes tipos de mole.":"Oaxaca is known for its wide variety of food traditions and its many types of mole.","Los chapulines tostados forman parte de la alimentación tradicional de varias comunidades de Oaxaca.":"Toasted grasshoppers (chapulines) are part of the traditional diet of several communities in Oaxaca.","Comí una empanada y quemé mi lengua.":"I ate an empanada and burned my tongue.","Comí empanadas frente a casas de colores.":"I ate empanadas in front of colorful houses.","Comí empanadas cerca de Caminito.":"I ate empanadas near Caminito.","Escuché música mientras buscaba mi cámara.":"I heard music while looking for my camera.","Escuché un bandoneón en plena calle.":"I heard a bandoneón right in the street.","Escuché tango junto a las casas de chapa pintada.":"I heard tango next to the painted tin houses.","Vi una casa pintada de tres colores.":"I saw a house painted in three colors.","Vi una pareja bailar sobre la acera.":"I saw a couple dance on the sidewalk.","Vi bailarines frente a los balcones de colores.":"I saw dancers in front of the colorful balconies.","Llevaba zapatos cómodos para caminar.":"I wore comfortable walking shoes.","Llevaba una foto de una calle muy colorida.":"I had a photo of a very colorful street.","Llevaba una camiseta azul y amarilla.":"I wore a blue and yellow jersey.","Me fui cuando empezó a soplar viento frío.":"I left when a cold wind started blowing.","Me fui cuando empezó la siguiente clase de tango.":"I left when the next tango class began.","Me fui cuando cerraron los puestos de Caminito.":"I left when the Caminito stalls closed.","Estaba en una calle llena de turistas.":"I was on a street full of tourists.","Estaba frente a casas de muchos colores.":"I was in front of brightly colored houses.","Estaba en Caminito, junto a una pareja de tango.":"I was on Caminito, next to a tango couple.","Estaba tomando fotos.":"I was taking photos.","Estaba retrocediendo para que saliera todo.":"I was backing up to fit everything in the shot.","Estaba aplaudiendo a unos bailarines de tango.":"I was applauding some tango dancers.","La Boca en Buenos Aires":"La Boca in Buenos Aires","Un turista intenta fotografiar tres casas pintadas de amarillo, azul y rojo mientras una pareja baila tango en la calle. El fotógrafo retrocede para mejorar el ángulo y casi se sienta sobre una caja de recuerdos. El detective recomienda mirar detrás antes de buscar la foto perfecta.":"A tourist tries to photograph three houses painted yellow, blue and red while a couple dances tango in the street. The photographer backs up for a better angle and nearly sits on a box of souvenirs. The detective recommends looking behind you before chasing the perfect photo.","Un músico toca el bandoneón, un instrumento parecido a un acordeón pequeño, mientras los bailarines marcan el ritmo sobre la acera. Un niño pregunta si él también puede aprender a bailar. Una bailarina le toma la mano y, en un minuto, ya está recibiendo su primera clase. Su padre apenas alcanza a sacar la cámara.":"A musician plays the bandoneón, an instrument like a small accordion, while the dancers tap out the rhythm on the sidewalk. A boy asks if he can learn to dance too. A dancer takes his hand and, within a minute, he's getting his first lesson. His father barely gets the camera out in time.","El olor de las empanadas recién horneadas sale de un pequeño restaurante. Un visitante guarda su cámara y muerde una empanada de carne, pero el relleno está tan caliente que se quema la lengua. El detective identifica al principal sospechoso: la falta de paciencia.":"The smell of freshly baked empanadas comes from a small restaurant. A visitor puts away his camera and bites into a beef empanada, but the filling is so hot he burns his tongue. The detective identifies the main suspect: impatience.","La Boca es un barrio de Buenos Aires conocido por sus casas de colores y su historia de inmigración.":"La Boca is a Buenos Aires neighborhood known for its colorful houses and its history of immigration.","Caminito es una calle museo famosa por sus edificios pintados y sus espectáculos artísticos.":"Caminito is a street-museum famous for its painted buildings and street performances.","Comí un bocadillo y una paloma pidió la mitad.":"I ate a sandwich and a pigeon asked for half.","Comí un bocadillo de calamares recién hecho.":"I ate a freshly made calamari sandwich.","Comí calamares bajo los arcos de la plaza.":"I ate calamari under the arches of the square.","Escuché una guitarra bajo unos arcos.":"I heard a guitar under some arches.","Escuché las tazas de una terraza bajo los arcos.":"I heard cups clinking at a café terrace under the arches.","Escuché música junto a la estatua de Felipe III.":"I heard music next to the statue of Philip III.","Vi una estatua de un hombre a caballo.":"I saw a statue of a man on a horse.","Vi a Felipe III montado en su caballo de bronce.":"I saw Philip III riding his bronze horse.","Vi los balcones rojos de la Casa de la Panadería.":"I saw the red balconies of the Casa de la Panadería.","Llevaba un mapa lleno de calles pequeñas.":"I had a map full of little streets.","Llevaba una bolsa de una tienda de recuerdos.":"I had a bag from a souvenir shop.","Llevaba una foto de la estatua ecuestre.":"I had a photo of the equestrian statue.","Me fui cuando el sol calentó demasiado.":"I left when the sun got too hot.","Me fui porque una paloma vigilaba mi almuerzo.":"I left because a pigeon was watching my lunch.","Me fui por la calle de Toledo buscando churros.":"I left down Calle de Toledo looking for churros.","Estaba en una plaza con terrazas.":"I was in a square full of café terraces.","Estaba bajo unos soportales de piedra.":"I was under some stone arcades.","Estaba junto a la estatua de Felipe III.":"I was next to the statue of Philip III.","Estaba tomando un café.":"I was having a coffee.","Estaba buscando sitio en una terraza.":"I was looking for a seat on a terrace.","Estaba comiendo un bocadillo de calamares.":"I was eating a calamari sandwich.","La Plaza Mayor de Madrid":"Madrid's Plaza Mayor","Un camarero cruza la plaza con una bandeja de cafés mientras un turista busca la estatua de Felipe III. La encuentra en el centro, pero primero fotografía tres palomas que parecen convencidas de ser las verdaderas protagonistas.":"A waiter crosses the square with a tray of coffees while a tourist looks for the statue of Philip III. He finds it in the middle, but first he photographs three pigeons that seem convinced they're the real stars.","Las tazas chocan suavemente en las mesas de una terraza. Un músico toca la guitarra bajo los arcos y una pareja discute qué calle tomar. El detective observa que ambos tienen un mapa y ninguno parece dispuesto a usarlo.":"Cups clink softly on the tables of a café terrace. A musician plays guitar under the arches and a couple argues about which street to take. The detective notes that both have a map and neither seems willing to use it.","El olor de un bocadillo de calamares recién preparado sale de un restaurante cercano. Un visitante abre una servilleta para comer, pero una paloma se acerca con demasiada confianza. La investigación se convierte en una defensa del almuerzo.":"The smell of a freshly made calamari sandwich comes from a nearby restaurant. A visitor unfolds a napkin to eat, but a pigeon approaches with far too much confidence. The investigation turns into a defense of lunch.","La Plaza Mayor de Madrid fue construida principalmente durante el reinado de Felipe III, a comienzos del siglo XVII.":"Madrid's Plaza Mayor was built mainly during the reign of Philip III, in the early 17th century.","La estatua ecuestre de Felipe III fue colocada en el centro de la plaza en 1848.":"The equestrian statue of Philip III was placed in the center of the square in 1848.","Comí pescado frito junto al mar.":"I ate fried fish by the sea.","Comí una arepa de huevo y pedí otra servilleta.":"I ate an arepa de huevo and asked for another napkin.","Comí arepa de huevo frente a la muralla.":"I ate an arepa de huevo in front of the city wall.","Escuché ruedas sobre calles de piedra.":"I heard wheels on stone streets.","Escuché música junto a las murallas antiguas.":"I heard music by the old city walls.","Escuché música cerca de la Torre del Reloj.":"I heard music near the Clock Tower.","Vi balcones llenos de flores.":"I saw balconies full of flowers.","Vi una vendedora con frutas sobre la cabeza.":"I saw a vendor carrying fruit on her head.","Vi balcones coloniales y vendedores de frutas.":"I saw colonial balconies and fruit vendors.","Llevaba un sombrero que casi salió volando.":"I had a hat that almost flew away.","Llevaba una botella de agua casi vacía.":"I had a nearly empty water bottle.","Llevaba una foto del Castillo de San Felipe.":"I had a photo of the San Felipe Castle.","Me fui porque el calor ganó la discusión.":"I left because the heat won the argument.","Me fui cuando el sol cayó detrás del mar.":"I left when the sun went down behind the sea.","Me fui al anochecer por la Puerta del Reloj.":"I left at dusk through the Clock Gate.","Estaba en una ciudad junto al mar.":"I was in a city by the sea.","Estaba en una calle con balcones de flores.":"I was on a street with flower-covered balconies.","Estaba sobre la muralla, mirando el atardecer.":"I was on top of the city wall, watching the sunset.","Estaba caminando sin prisa.":"I was walking without hurrying.","Estaba comprando fruta a una palenquera.":"I was buying fruit from a palenquera.","Estaba fotografiando el sol sobre el Caribe.":"I was photographing the sun over the Caribbean.","Cartagena de Indias al atardecer":"Cartagena de Indias at sunset","Una vendedora lleva una bandeja de frutas sobre la cabeza mientras camina junto a una muralla de piedra. Un turista intenta fotografiar el sol sobre el mar, pero su sombrero sale volando. El detective registra que el viento también quiere participar en las vacaciones.":"A vendor carries a tray of fruit on her head as she walks along a stone wall. A tourist tries to photograph the sun over the sea, but his hat flies off. The detective records that the wind also wants to join the vacation.","Las ruedas de un coche de caballos pasan sobre los adoquines mientras un músico toca una melodía en una esquina. Una familia pregunta cuánto falta para llegar al restaurante. El hijo menor responde que lleva preguntando lo mismo desde hace veinte minutos.":"The wheels of a horse-drawn carriage roll over the cobblestones while a musician plays a tune on a corner. A family asks how much longer until the restaurant. The youngest son replies that he's been asking the same thing for twenty minutes.","El aroma del pescado frito y las arepas de huevo llega desde una cocina cercana. Un visitante sostiene una botella de agua fría mientras busca una mesa a la sombra. El detective concluye que el calor puede resolver cualquier discusión sobre dónde cenar.":"The aroma of fried fish and arepas de huevo drifts from a nearby kitchen. A visitor holds a cold bottle of water while looking for a table in the shade. The detective concludes that heat can settle any argument about where to have dinner.","Cartagena de Indias fue fundada en 1533 y se convirtió en un importante puerto del Caribe.":"Cartagena de Indias was founded in 1533 and became an important Caribbean port.","El puerto, las fortalezas y el conjunto monumental de Cartagena forman parte del Patrimonio Mundial de la UNESCO desde 1984.":"Cartagena's port, fortresses and historic center have been a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1984.","Comí pastel y escondí otra porción.":"I ate cake and hid another slice.","Comí pastel después de un baile muy elegante.":"I ate cake after a very elegant dance.","Comí pastel junto a quince velas decorativas.":"I ate cake next to fifteen decorative candles.","Escuché música hasta que me dolieron los pies.":"I heard music until my feet hurt.","Escuché al DJ anunciar un baile especial.":"I heard the DJ announce a special dance.","Escuché anunciar el vals de la quinceañera.":"I heard them announce the quinceañera's waltz.","Vi a una familia tomar cien fotografías.":"I saw a family take a hundred photos.","Vi un vestido enorme bajar por la escalera.":"I saw a huge dress come down the stairs.","Vi a la festejada bailar con su padre.":"I saw the birthday girl dance with her father.","Llevaba zapatos que parecían instrumentos de tortura.":"I wore shoes that felt like torture devices.","Llevaba flores para la joven de la fiesta.":"I brought flowers for the girl of the party.","Llevaba un regalo para sus quince años.":"I brought a gift for her fifteenth birthday.","Me fui cuando mis pies pidieron ayuda.":"I left when my feet begged for help.","Me fui después del baile con su papá.":"I left after the dance with her dad.","Me fui después de la última foto familiar.":"I left after the last family photo.","Estaba en un salón de fiestas.":"I was in a party hall.","Estaba en una mesa cerca de la pista.":"I was at a table near the dance floor.","Estaba junto a la escalera, esperando a la festejada.":"I was by the staircase, waiting for the birthday girl.","Estaba bailando un poco.":"I was dancing a little.","Estaba aplaudiendo el vals con su padre.":"I was applauding the waltz with her father.","Estaba en la fila para la foto con la quinceañera.":"I was in line for the photo with the quinceañera.","Una fiesta de quince años":"A quinceañera party","Una joven con un vestido elegante intenta bajar una escalera sin pisar la falda. Su prima sostiene el ramo de flores y su padre espera para bailar. El detective sospecha que el vestido necesita su propio equipo de seguridad.":"A young woman in an elegant dress tries to come down a staircase without stepping on her skirt. Her cousin holds the bouquet and her father waits to dance. The detective suspects the dress needs its own security team.","El DJ anuncia el siguiente baile mientras los invitados aplauden. Una tía busca a tres primos para una foto familiar, pero uno está escondido detrás de la mesa de postres. El detective conoce perfectamente ese escondite.":"The DJ announces the next dance while the guests applaud. An aunt is looking for three cousins for a family photo, but one is hiding behind the dessert table. The detective knows that hiding spot very well.","El pastel de vainilla y las flores decorativas llenan el salón de aromas dulces. Un invitado sostiene un plato de arroz y pollo mientras observa la mesa de dulces. El detective calcula que todavía queda espacio para dos porciones de pastel.":"Vanilla cake and decorative flowers fill the hall with sweet scents. A guest holds a plate of rice and chicken while eyeing the dessert table. The detective calculates there's still room for two slices of cake.","La celebración de los quince años marca tradicionalmente una etapa importante en la vida de una joven en muchas comunidades latinoamericanas.":"A quinceañera traditionally marks an important stage in a young woman's life in many Latin American communities.","Las costumbres pueden incluir un baile especial, una ceremonia religiosa o una reunión familiar, según la familia y la región.":"Customs can include a special dance, a religious ceremony or a family gathering, depending on the family and the region.","Comí algo caliente y me quemé la lengua.":"I ate something hot and burned my tongue.","Comí pan dulce antes de que saliera el sol.":"I ate sweet bread before sunrise.","Comí una pieza de pan dulce recién horneada.":"I ate a piece of freshly baked sweet bread.","Escuché una campanita al abrir la puerta.":"I heard a little bell when the door opened.","Escuché bandejas metálicas salir del horno.":"I heard metal trays come out of the oven.","Escuché al panadero sacar la primera bandeja.":"I heard the baker pull out the first tray.","Vi a un señor bostezar frente al mostrador.":"I saw a man yawning at the counter.","Vi al panadero cubierto de harina.":"I saw the baker covered in flour.","Vi el reloj marcar las seis junto al horno.":"I saw the clock strike six next to the oven.","Llevaba una bolsa de papel casi vacía.":"I had an almost empty paper bag.","Llevaba café y una bolsa de pan caliente.":"I had coffee and a bag of warm bread.","Llevaba una bolsa de bolillos todavía calientes.":"I had a bag of bolillos, still warm.","Me fui porque mi autobús estaba llegando.":"I left because my bus was coming.","Me fui cuando comenzó a formarse una fila.":"I left when a line started to form.","Me fui antes del amanecer con pan y café.":"I left before dawn with bread and coffee.","Estaba en una tienda pequeña.":"I was in a small shop.","Estaba frente a una vitrina llena de pan.":"I was in front of a display case full of bread.","Estaba junto al horno, a las seis de la mañana.":"I was next to the oven at six in the morning.","Estaba haciendo un mandado.":"I was running an errand.","Estaba eligiendo pan con pinzas y una charola.":"I was choosing bread with tongs and a tray.","Estaba comprando pan dulce recién horneado.":"I was buying freshly baked sweet bread.","Una panadería a las seis de la mañana":"A bakery at six in the morning","Un panadero abre el horno y saca una bandeja de panes dulces cubiertos de azúcar. Un cliente todavía medio dormido señala tres piezas, pero el panadero entiende cinco. El detective considera que el error favorece claramente al cliente.":"A baker opens the oven and pulls out a tray of sugar-covered sweet rolls. A half-asleep customer points to three pieces, but the baker hears five. The detective considers the mistake clearly in the customer's favor.","Una campanita suena cuando se abre la puerta. Las pinzas metálicas chocan contra una bandeja y la máquina de café comienza a trabajar. Un hombre bosteza tan fuerte que casi interrumpe el pedido de la siguiente persona.":"A little bell rings when the door opens. Metal tongs clink against a tray and the coffee machine gets to work. A man yawns so loudly he almost interrupts the next person's order.","El aroma del pan recién horneado se mezcla con canela y café caliente. Una estudiante sostiene una mochila y una bolsa de papel, pero decide salir temprano cuando descubre que el autobús está llegando.":"The aroma of fresh bread mixes with cinnamon and hot coffee. A student holds a backpack and a paper bag, but decides to leave early when she sees her bus coming.","El pan dulce tiene muchas variedades regionales en América Latina.":"Sweet bread (pan dulce) has many regional varieties across Latin America.","En México existen cientos de variedades de pan dulce, muchas con nombres curiosos como orejas, besos o cuernitos.":"Mexico has hundreds of kinds of pan dulce, many with funny names like orejas (ears), besos (kisses) or cuernitos (little horns).","Comí pollo con salsa y manché mi camisa.":"I ate chicken in sauce and stained my shirt.","Comí mole mientras sonaban las trompetas.":"I ate mole while the trumpets played.","Comí mole mientras el mariachi tocaba.":"I ate mole while the mariachi played.","Escuché una canción que todos conocían.":"I heard a song everyone knew.","Escuché violines y guitarras junto a la pista.":"I heard violins and guitars by the dance floor.","Escuché trompetas durante el primer baile.":"I heard trumpets during the first dance.","Vi a una pareja bailar entre las mesas.":"I saw a couple dancing between the tables.","Vi músicos con sombreros grandes y elegantes.":"I saw musicians in big, elegant hats.","Vi a los novios bailar frente a los mariachis.":"I saw the newlyweds dance in front of the mariachis.","Llevaba una cámara y olvidé tomar fotos.":"I brought a camera and forgot to take photos.","Llevaba un regalo para los recién casados.":"I brought a gift for the newlyweds.","Llevaba una foto del grupo con trajes de charro.":"I had a photo of the band in charro suits.","Me fui cuando mis zapatos dejaron de cooperar.":"I left when my shoes stopped cooperating.","Me fui después de una canción muy romántica.":"I left after a very romantic song.","Me fui cuando terminó la serenata de los novios.":"I left when the couple's serenade ended.","Estaba en una mesa redonda.":"I was at a round table.","Estaba cerca de la pista de baile.":"I was near the dance floor.","Estaba al lado de los mariachis.":"I was right next to the mariachis.","Estaba celebrando con la familia.":"I was celebrating with the family.","Estaba cantando con toda el alma.":"I was singing my heart out.","Estaba pidiéndoles otra canción a los mariachis.":"I was asking the mariachis for another song.","Una boda con mariachi":"A wedding with mariachi","Los recién casados caminan entre las mesas mientras un músico con traje de charro ajusta su sombrero. Un niño lleva los anillos de recuerdo en una pequeña caja y anuncia que ahora es responsable de la seguridad de las joyas.":"The newlyweds walk between the tables while a musician in a charro suit adjusts his hat. A boy carries the keepsake rings in a small box and announces that he is now in charge of jewelry security.","Las trompetas comienzan una canción alegre mientras los invitados aplauden. Una abuela reconoce la melodía y empieza a cantar antes que los músicos. El detective sospecha que ella conoce todas las canciones del repertorio.":"The trumpets start a cheerful song while the guests applaud. A grandmother recognizes the melody and starts singing before the musicians do. The detective suspects she knows every song in the repertoire.","El aroma del mole y las tortillas calientes llega desde la cocina. Un invitado sostiene una cámara y un plato al mismo tiempo, pero decide dejar de tomar fotografías cuando la salsa amenaza con caer sobre su camisa.":"The aroma of mole and warm tortillas comes from the kitchen. A guest holds a camera and a plate at the same time, but decides to stop taking photos when the sauce threatens to land on his shirt.","El mariachi es una tradición musical de México reconocida por la UNESCO como Patrimonio Cultural Inmaterial de la Humanidad desde 2011.":"Mariachi is a Mexican musical tradition recognized by UNESCO as Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity since 2011.","Los grupos de mariachi modernos suelen incluir violines, trompetas, guitarras, vihuela y guitarrón.":"Modern mariachi groups usually include violins, trumpets, guitars, vihuela and guitarrón.","Comí una empanada durante el descanso.":"I ate an empanada at halftime.","Comí empanadas junto a la cancha de tierra.":"I ate empanadas next to the dirt field.","Comí una empanada después de meter un gol.":"I ate an empanada after scoring a goal.","Escuché a un papá gritar instrucciones.":"I heard a dad shouting instructions.","Escuché un silbato y muchas protestas.":"I heard a whistle and lots of complaining.","Escuché gritar ¡gol! junto a dos mochilas.":"I heard someone yell 'goal!' next to two backpacks.","Vi a un perro correr detrás de los niños.":"I saw a dog running after the kids.","Vi dos mochilas marcando la meta.":"I saw two backpacks marking the goal.","Vi al portero lanzarse sobre la tierra.":"I saw the goalie dive into the dirt.","Llevaba una botella de agua y una gorra.":"I had a water bottle and a cap.","Llevaba zapatos deportivos llenos de polvo.":"I wore sneakers covered in dust.","Llevaba una pelota vieja bajo el brazo.":"I had an old ball under my arm.","Me fui cuando comenzó a llover.":"I left when it started to rain.","Me fui cuando un perro robó el balón.":"I left when a dog stole the ball.","Me fui cuando terminó el partido del barrio.":"I left when the neighborhood game ended.","Estaba en la calle, con los vecinos.":"I was in the street with the neighbors.","Estaba sentado en la acera, mirando.":"I was sitting on the sidewalk, watching.","Estaba junto a una portería hecha con mochilas.":"I was next to a goal made of backpacks.","Estaba pasando la tarde.":"I was spending the afternoon.","Estaba gritando '¡pásala!' sin parar.":"I was yelling 'pass it!' nonstop.","Estaba persiguiendo al perro que se llevó la pelota.":"I was chasing the dog that took the ball.","Un partido de fútbol del barrio":"A neighborhood soccer game","Un niño corre detrás de una pelota mientras su compañero defiende una portería marcada con dos mochilas. Un perro aparece en medio de la cancha y se lleva la pelota. El detective declara que el nuevo jugador tiene cuatro patas y ninguna intención de respetar las reglas.":"A boy runs after a ball while his teammate defends a goal marked with two backpacks. A dog appears in the middle of the field and runs off with the ball. The detective declares that the new player has four legs and no intention of following the rules.","Un silbato anuncia el comienzo del segundo tiempo mientras los espectadores gritan desde la sombra. Un padre asegura que el balón salió de la cancha. El otro responde que no. El detective solicita una repetición en cámara lenta, pero nadie tiene una.":"A whistle signals the start of the second half while the spectators shout from the shade. One dad insists the ball went out. Another says it didn't. The detective requests a slow-motion replay, but nobody has one.","El aroma de las empanadas llega desde un puesto cercano. Una jugadora bebe agua de su botella mientras observa cómo el perro sigue corriendo con la pelota. El equipo decide hacer una pausa hasta recuperar el equipo deportivo.":"The smell of empanadas comes from a nearby stand. A player drinks from her water bottle while watching the dog keep running with the ball. The team decides to take a break until they get their equipment back.","El fútbol se juega normalmente con once jugadores por equipo en los partidos oficiales.":"In official matches, soccer is normally played with eleven players per team.","En los partidos informales, las reglas, el número de jugadores y el tamaño de la cancha pueden adaptarse al espacio disponible.":"In informal games, the rules, the number of players and the size of the field can be adapted to the space available.","Comí tanto que no pude probar el postre.":"I ate so much I couldn't try dessert.","Comí polvorones y terminé cubierto de azúcar.":"I ate polvorones and ended up covered in sugar.","Comí mantecados y polvorones andaluces.":"I ate Andalusian mantecados and polvorones.","Escuché a mis primos cantar en el salón.":"I heard my cousins singing in the living room.","Escuché villancicos con palmas y panderetas.":"I heard carols with clapping and tambourines.","Escuché zambombas y villancicos de Navidad.":"I heard zambombas and Christmas carols.","Vi a mi abuela vigilar una olla enorme.":"I saw my grandma guarding a huge pot.","Vi una mesa llena de turrón y mantecados.":"I saw a table full of turrón and mantecados.","Vi un belén junto a una mesa de turrones.":"I saw a nativity scene next to a table of turrón.","Llevaba un regalo escondido en una bolsa.":"I had a present hidden in a bag.","Llevaba una caja de dulces para la familia.":"I brought a box of sweets for the family.","Llevaba una pandereta para cantar villancicos.":"I brought a tambourine to sing carols.","Me fui cuando los niños empezaron a dormirse.":"I left when the kids started falling asleep.","Me fui después de cantar junto al belén.":"I left after singing by the nativity scene.","Me fui después de la cena del 24 de diciembre.":"I left after the December 24th dinner.","Estaba en casa de la familia.":"I was at the family's house.","Estaba en la cocina, cerca del horno.":"I was in the kitchen, near the oven.","Estaba junto al belén, al lado de la zambomba.":"I was by the nativity scene, next to the zambomba.","Estaba ayudando a poner la mesa.":"I was helping set the table.","Estaba robando un langostino a escondidas.":"I was sneaking a prawn.","Estaba cantando villancicos con la zambomba.":"I was singing carols with the zambomba.","La cocina de la abuela en Nochebuena, en un pueblo de Andalucía":"Grandma's kitchen on Christmas Eve, in an Andalusian village","La abuela vigila una cazuela de barro con cordero al horno mientras su nieto intenta robar un langostino de la bandeja. Ella lo descubre sin siquiera darse la vuelta. El detective sospecha que las abuelas tienen un sistema de vigilancia más avanzado que cualquier cámara.":"Grandma watches over a clay pot of roast lamb while her grandson tries to steal a prawn from the platter. She catches him without even turning around. The detective suspects grandmothers have a surveillance system more advanced than any camera.","En el salón, los primos cantan villancicos con una zambomba y una botella de cristal que alguien rasca con una cuchara. A las nueve, el abuelo pide silencio para escuchar el mensaje del Rey en la televisión. Nadie le hace caso.":"In the living room, the cousins sing carols with a zambomba (a friction drum) and a glass bottle someone scrapes with a spoon. At nine, grandpa asks for silence to hear the King's message on TV. Nobody listens.","Huele a cordero asado, a sopa de almendras y a turrón recién partido. Una tía llega con una bandeja de polvorones y descubre que no queda sitio en la mesa. El detective propone mover el belén, pero nadie se atreve a tocar ni una sola oveja.":"It smells of roast lamb, almond soup and freshly broken turrón. An aunt arrives with a tray of polvorones and discovers there's no room left on the table. The detective suggests moving the nativity scene, but nobody dares touch a single sheep.","En España, muchas familias celebran la cena más importante de la Navidad la noche del 24 de diciembre, y los regalos tradicionales llegan el 6 de enero con los Reyes Magos.":"In Spain, many families have the most important Christmas dinner on the night of December 24, and the traditional gifts arrive on January 6 with the Three Kings.","El turrón, un dulce de almendra y miel, se fabrica en Jijona (Alicante) desde hace siglos.":"Turrón, a sweet made of almonds and honey, has been made in Jijona (Alicante) for centuries.","Comí fruta cerca del agua.":"I ate fruit near the water.","Comí una barra de cereal después de nadar.":"I ate a cereal bar after swimming.","Comí mientras un lobo marino dormía cerca.":"I ate while a sea lion slept nearby.","Escuché olas contra las rocas.":"I heard waves against the rocks.","Oí aves gritar junto a la costa.":"I heard birds screeching along the coast.","Escuché a un ave de patas azul brillante.":"I heard a bird with bright blue feet.","Vi a una guía explicar las reglas.":"I saw a guide explaining the rules.","Vi a un turista esquivar un animal dormido.":"I saw a tourist step around a sleeping animal.","Vi a una guía proteger a una iguana marina.":"I saw a guide protecting a marine iguana.","Llevaba una botella de agua.":"I had a bottle of water.","Llevaba zapatos para caminar sobre lava.":"I wore shoes for walking on lava.","Llevaba binoculares para ver aves de patas azules.":"I had binoculars to see blue-footed birds.","Me fui porque hacía mucho calor.":"I left because it was very hot.","Me fui antes de que saliera el barco.":"I left before the boat departed.","Me fui porque un lobo marino bloqueaba el paso.":"I left because a sea lion was blocking the path.","Estaba en una isla.":"I was on an island.","Estaba en un sendero sobre rocas negras.":"I was on a trail over black rocks.","Estaba en una playa junto a un lobo marino dormido.":"I was on a beach next to a sleeping sea lion.","Estaba mirando animales.":"I was watching animals.","Estaba caminando con cuidado para no molestar.":"I was walking carefully so I wouldn't disturb anything.","Estaba fotografiando una iguana marina.":"I was photographing a marine iguana.","Las Islas Galápagos junto a una playa volcánica":"The Galápagos Islands by a volcanic beach","Una iguana marina descansa sobre una roca negra mientras un lobo marino duerme cerca del sendero. Un visitante intenta pasar sin molestarlo, pero el animal ocupa todo el camino. El detective sospecha que aquí los animales tienen prioridad.":"A marine iguana rests on a black rock while a sea lion sleeps near the trail. A visitor tries to get past without disturbing it, but the animal takes up the whole path. The detective suspects that animals have the right of way here.","Las olas golpean las rocas y un ave marina silba desde la costa. Tiene las patas de un azul tan brillante que parecen pintadas. Una guía pide al grupo que mantenga la distancia. Un turista quiere preguntar si las patas son de verdad, pero una ráfaga de viento se lleva sus palabras y casi también su sombrero.":"Waves crash against the rocks and a seabird whistles from the shore. Its feet are such a bright blue they look painted. A guide asks the group to keep their distance. A tourist wants to ask if the feet are real, but a gust of wind carries off his words and nearly his hat too.","El aire salado se mezcla con el olor de las algas sobre las piedras calientes. Una viajera abre su mochila para sacar agua y una barra de cereal. El sol le quema los hombros, así que decide regresar al barco antes de terminar su merienda.":"The salty air mixes with the smell of seaweed on the hot stones. A traveler opens her backpack to take out water and a cereal bar. The sun is burning her shoulders, so she decides to head back to the boat before finishing her snack.","Las Islas Galápagos se encuentran a unos 1.000 kilómetros de la costa continental de Ecuador.":"The Galápagos Islands lie about 1,000 kilometers off the mainland coast of Ecuador.","Charles Darwin visitó las islas en 1835, y sus observaciones contribuyeron al desarrollo de sus ideas sobre la evolución.":"Charles Darwin visited the islands in 1835, and his observations helped shape his ideas about evolution.","Comí galletas durante la excursión.":"I ate cookies during the tour.","Tomé un té caliente para entrar en calor.":"I drank hot tea to warm up.","Comí mientras el cielo se reflejaba bajo mis pies.":"I ate while the sky reflected under my feet.","Escuché el viento junto al vehículo.":"I heard the wind by the vehicle.","Oí mis botas crujir sobre el suelo blanco.":"I heard my boots crunch on the white ground.","Escuché cristales de sal romperse bajo mis botas.":"I heard salt crystals crack under my boots.","Vi a un guía preparar una fotografía.":"I saw a guide setting up a photo.","Vi a una turista saltar sobre un reflejo.":"I saw a tourist jump over a reflection.","Vi a un guía usar figuras para fotos de perspectiva.":"I saw a guide use figurines for perspective photos.","Llevaba lentes oscuros y agua.":"I had sunglasses and water.","Llevaba botas para caminar sobre el agua.":"I wore boots for walking on water.","Llevaba lentes contra el brillo de la sal.":"I wore glasses against the glare of the salt.","Me fui porque tenía mucho frío.":"I left because I was very cold.","Me fui porque la luz me cansó los ojos.":"I left because the light tired my eyes.","Me fui cuando el cielo y el suelo parecían uno.":"I left when the sky and the ground looked like one.","Estaba en un lugar muy abierto.":"I was somewhere very open.","Estaba en una llanura completamente blanca.":"I was on a completely white plain.","Estaba sobre el salar, que reflejaba el cielo.":"I was on the salt flat, which reflected the sky.","Estaba haciendo fotos con perspectiva divertida.":"I was taking funny perspective photos.","Estaba saltando sobre un espejo de agua y sal.":"I was jumping on a mirror of water and salt.","El Salar de Uyuni después de la lluvia":"The Uyuni Salt Flat after the rain","Una capa delgada de agua refleja el cielo sobre una superficie blanca que parece no terminar nunca. Un turista intenta fotografiar a su amiga saltando entre las nubes reflejadas. Ella aterriza en un charco y descubre que sus zapatos no son tan impermeables como prometía la caja.":"A thin layer of water reflects the sky over a white surface that seems to go on forever. A tourist tries to photograph her friend jumping between the reflected clouds. She lands in a puddle and discovers her shoes aren't as waterproof as the box promised.","Las botas crujen sobre los cristales secos cerca del vehículo. Un guía llama al grupo para regresar antes de que cambie el tiempo. Un visitante sigue buscando el horizonte, pero el detective sospecha que el horizonte se ha escondido.":"Boots crunch on the dry crystals near the vehicle. A guide calls the group back before the weather changes. One visitor keeps searching for the horizon, but the detective suspects the horizon has gone into hiding.","El aire frío y seco entra por la nariz mientras una viajera abre un termo de té caliente y una bolsa de galletas. La luz reflejada le obliga a ponerse lentes oscuros. Después de diez minutos, decide que sus ojos necesitan vacaciones de las vacaciones.":"Cold, dry air fills her nose as a traveler opens a thermos of hot tea and a bag of cookies. The reflected light forces her to put on sunglasses. After ten minutes, she decides her eyes need a vacation from the vacation.","El Salar de Uyuni es el salar más grande del mundo y ocupa aproximadamente 10.500 kilómetros cuadrados.":"The Salar de Uyuni is the largest salt flat in the world, covering about 10,500 square kilometers.","Durante la temporada de lluvias, una capa de agua puede convertir su superficie en un enorme reflejo del cielo.":"During the rainy season, a layer of water can turn its surface into a giant mirror of the sky.","Comí arroz durante un descanso.":"I ate rice during a break.","Comí gallo pinto antes de caminar.":"I ate gallo pinto before the hike.","Comí gallo pinto antes de buscar perezosos.":"I ate gallo pinto before looking for sloths.","Escuché animales entre los árboles.":"I heard animals in the trees.","Oí un grito muy fuerte sobre mi cabeza.":"I heard a very loud scream above my head.","Escuché a un mono aullador desde las ramas.":"I heard a howler monkey from the branches.","Vi a una guía señalar un árbol.":"I saw a guide point at a tree.","Vi a un turista limpiar sus lentes mojados.":"I saw a tourist wipe his wet glasses.","Vi a una guía seguir hormigas cortadoras.":"I saw a guide following leafcutter ants.","Llevaba una mochila y agua.":"I had a backpack and water.","Llevaba binoculares y un impermeable.":"I had binoculars and a raincoat.","Llevaba lentes para buscar monos y perezosos.":"I had glasses to look for monkeys and sloths.","Me fui porque empezó a llover.":"I left because it started to rain.","Me fui porque mis calcetines no se secaban.":"I left because my socks wouldn't dry.","Me fui después de oír otro mono aullador.":"I left after hearing another howler monkey.","Estaba en un sendero.":"I was on a trail.","Estaba bajo árboles altísimos y húmedos.":"I was under huge, damp trees.","Estaba debajo de un perezoso colgado de una rama.":"I was under a sloth hanging from a branch.","Estaba caminando con calma.":"I was walking calmly.","Estaba espantando mosquitos sin éxito.":"I was swatting mosquitoes, unsuccessfully.","Estaba siguiendo una fila de hormigas cortadoras.":"I was following a line of leafcutter ants.","Una caminata por la selva de Costa Rica":"A hike through the Costa Rican rainforest","Un perezoso cuelga de una rama mientras una fila de hormigas cortadoras de hojas cruza el sendero. Un visitante se agacha para tomar una foto y descubre que sus lentes se han empañado otra vez. El detective sospecha que la humedad está trabajando para el enemigo.":"A sloth hangs from a branch while a line of leafcutter ants crosses the trail. A visitor crouches to take a photo and finds his glasses have fogged up again. The detective suspects the humidity is working for the enemy.","Un mono aullador lanza un grito tan fuerte que un turista casi deja caer sus binoculares. La guía sonríe y señala las copas de los árboles. El detective anota que el sospechoso pesa mucho menos de lo que su voz hace pensar.":"A howler monkey lets out a scream so loud a tourist nearly drops his binoculars. The guide smiles and points to the treetops. The detective notes that the suspect weighs much less than his voice suggests.","La tierra mojada y las hojas verdes llenan el aire. Una viajera abre una bolsa con gallo pinto para comer durante el descanso, pero empieza a llover. Guarda la comida, se pone el impermeable y descubre que sus calcetines ya estaban mojados.":"Wet earth and green leaves fill the air. A traveler opens a bag of gallo pinto to eat during the break, but it starts to rain. She puts the food away, puts on her raincoat and discovers her socks were already wet.","Costa Rica alberga más de 900 especies de aves registradas.":"Costa Rica is home to more than 900 recorded bird species.","Los monos aulladores producen llamadas que pueden escucharse a varios kilómetros de distancia.":"Howler monkeys make calls that can be heard several kilometers away.","Comí un sándwich durante la caminata.":"I ate a sandwich during the hike.","Comí chocolate para recuperar energía.":"I ate chocolate to get my energy back.","Comí mientras el viento movía mi mochila.":"I ate while the wind shook my backpack.","Escuché el viento contra mi chaqueta.":"I heard the wind against my jacket.","Oí ráfagas que tapaban la voz del guía.":"I heard gusts that drowned out the guide's voice.","Escuché el viento rugir entre montañas y hielo.":"I heard the wind roar between mountains and ice.","Vi a un excursionista con bastones.":"I saw a hiker with trekking poles.","Vi a una turista perseguir su gorro.":"I saw a tourist chasing her hat.","Vi a un guía señalar un cóndor sobre el valle.":"I saw a guide point to a condor over the valley.","Llevaba guantes y una chaqueta.":"I had gloves and a jacket.","Llevaba bastones y un gorro bien ajustado.":"I had trekking poles and a tight hat.","Llevaba una correa para que no volara mi gorro.":"I had a strap so my hat wouldn't fly away.","Me fui porque tenía las manos frías.":"I left because my hands were cold.","Me fui cuando casi perdí mi sombrero.":"I left when I almost lost my hat.","Me fui antes de que el viento robara mi mochila.":"I left before the wind could steal my backpack.","Estaba al aire libre.":"I was outdoors.","Estaba en un sendero entre montañas.":"I was on a trail between mountains.","Estaba frente a un glaciar, luchando contra el viento.":"I was in front of a glacier, fighting the wind.","Estaba caminando bastante.":"I was walking a lot.","Estaba sujetando mi gorro con las dos manos.":"I was holding my hat with both hands.","Estaba persiguiendo mi gorro cuesta abajo.":"I was chasing my hat downhill.","Un sendero de la Patagonia con viento fuerte":"A windy trail in Patagonia","Un excursionista intenta sujetar su gorro mientras camina frente a montañas de roca y hielo. Una ráfaga se lo arranca de la cabeza y lo manda cuesta abajo. El detective observa la persecución y decide que ningún sombrero merece tanto esfuerzo.":"A hiker tries to hold on to his hat as he walks past mountains of rock and ice. A gust rips it off his head and sends it downhill. The detective watches the chase and decides no hat is worth that much effort.","El viento golpea la capucha de una chaqueta y casi tapa las palabras del guía. Un cóndor pasa sobre el valle mientras alguien pregunta cuánto falta. La respuesta llega en tres partes, separadas por ráfagas.":"The wind slaps the hood of a jacket and nearly drowns out the guide's words. A condor glides over the valley while someone asks how much farther it is. The answer arrives in three parts, separated by gusts.","El aire frío trae olor a tierra húmeda y vegetación baja. Una caminante intenta comer un sándwich de queso, pero el papel comienza a volar. Guarda el almuerzo, ajusta los bastones y propone regresar antes de perder también la mochila.":"The cold air carries the smell of damp earth and low shrubs. A hiker tries to eat a cheese sandwich, but the wrapper starts flying away. She puts lunch away, adjusts her poles and suggests turning back before they lose the backpack too.","La Patagonia se extiende por el sur de Argentina y Chile.":"Patagonia stretches across southern Argentina and Chile.","Los fuertes vientos de la región están relacionados con los vientos del oeste que circulan por las latitudes medias del hemisferio sur.":"The region's strong winds are linked to the westerly winds that circle the middle latitudes of the Southern Hemisphere.","Comí algo rápido durante la visita.":"I ate something quick during the visit.","Comí chipá cerca de una pasarela.":"I ate chipá near a walkway.","Comí chipá mientras el agua rugía cerca.":"I ate chipá while the water roared nearby.","Escuché agua caer con mucha fuerza.":"I heard water falling with great force.","Oí un ruido que tapaba todas las voces.":"I heard a noise that drowned out every voice.","Escuché el rugido de la Garganta del Diablo.":"I heard the roar of the Devil's Throat.","Vi a una guía señalar el camino.":"I saw a guide pointing the way.","Vi a un turista proteger su cámara del agua.":"I saw a tourist protecting his camera from the water.","Vi a una guía empapada junto a la pasarela.":"I saw a soaked guide next to the walkway.","Llevaba una botella y mi teléfono.":"I had a bottle and my phone.","Llevaba una funda impermeable para la cámara.":"I had a waterproof case for my camera.","Llevaba una capa contra el agua de los saltos.":"I had a poncho against the spray from the falls.","Me fui porque estaba empapado.":"I left because I was soaked.","Me fui porque no podía escuchar a mi familia.":"I left because I couldn't hear my family.","Me fui después de ver la Garganta del Diablo.":"I left after seeing the Devil's Throat.","Estaba en un parque natural.":"I was in a nature park.","Estaba en una pasarela metálica.":"I was on a metal walkway.","Estaba frente a la Garganta del Diablo.":"I was in front of the Devil's Throat.","Estaba mirando el paisaje.":"I was looking at the scenery.","Estaba secando la pantalla de mi teléfono.":"I was drying my phone screen.","Estaba empapado por la nube de agua de la cascada.":"I was soaked by the waterfall's cloud of spray.","Las cataratas del Iguazú desde una pasarela":"Iguazú Falls from a walkway","Una enorme cortina de agua cae frente a una pasarela metálica. Un visitante levanta su teléfono para tomar una foto, pero una nube de gotas cubre la pantalla. El detective sospecha que el paisaje no quiere dejar pruebas.":"A huge curtain of water falls in front of a metal walkway. A visitor raises his phone to take a photo, but a cloud of droplets covers the screen. The detective suspects the scenery doesn't want to leave evidence.","El rugido del agua es tan fuerte que una guía debe señalar el camino con las manos. Un turista intenta hacer una pregunta y solo recibe una sonrisa. El detective recomienda escribir mensajes, aunque el papel tampoco duraría mucho.":"The roar of the water is so loud that a guide has to point the way with her hands. A tourist tries to ask a question and only gets a smile. The detective recommends writing notes, although paper wouldn't last long either.","El aire huele a vegetación mojada y agua fresca. Una familia guarda sus chipás en una mochila para protegerlos de las gotas. Un niño descubre que tiene los calcetines empapados y anuncia que ya está listo para regresar al hotel.":"The air smells of wet plants and fresh water. A family tucks their chipá into a backpack to protect them from the spray. A boy discovers his socks are soaked and announces he's ready to go back to the hotel.","Las cataratas del Iguazú se encuentran en la frontera entre Argentina y Brasil.":"The Iguazú Falls are on the border between Argentina and Brazil.","El sistema tiene aproximadamente 275 saltos de agua, aunque el número visible puede cambiar según el nivel del río.":"The system has about 275 waterfalls, although the number you can see changes with the river level.","Comí galletas bajo un árbol.":"I ate cookies under a tree.","Comí después de caminar entre piedras antiguas.":"I ate after walking among ancient stones.","Comí mientras esperaba la serpiente de luz.":"I ate while waiting for the serpent of light.","Escuché a una guía contar historias.":"I heard a guide telling stories.","Oí un eco extraño después de un aplauso.":"I heard a strange echo after a clap.","Escuché aplausos frente a la gran escalinata.":"I heard applause in front of the great staircase.","Vi a una guía señalar una pared.":"I saw a guide point at a wall.","Vi a turistas esperar una sombra especial.":"I saw tourists waiting for a special shadow.","Vi a una guía explicar la serpiente de luz.":"I saw a guide explain the serpent of light.","Llevaba agua y un sombrero.":"I had water and a hat.","Llevaba un folleto sobre una ciudad antigua.":"I had a brochure about an ancient city.","Llevaba una foto de la escalinata de Kukulkán.":"I had a photo of the staircase of Kukulkán.","Me fui porque el sol calentaba mucho.":"I left because the sun was very hot.","Me fui después de observar las sombras.":"I left after watching the shadows.","Me fui cuando desapareció la serpiente de luz.":"I left when the serpent of light disappeared.","Estaba en un sitio arqueológico.":"I was at an archaeological site.","Estaba en una explanada con mucha gente.":"I was on a wide esplanade with lots of people.","Estaba frente a la escalinata de El Castillo.":"I was in front of the staircase of El Castillo.","Estaba escuchando a un guía.":"I was listening to a guide.","Estaba esperando a que bajara el sol.":"I was waiting for the sun to go down.","Estaba viendo bajar la sombra de la serpiente.":"I was watching the serpent's shadow descend.","Chichén Itzá cerca del equinoccio":"Chichén Itzá near the equinox","La luz del sol forma una serie de triángulos de sombra sobre la gran escalinata de piedra. Un guía señala la figura que parece bajar por el costado del edificio. Un visitante intenta fotografiarla, pero descubre que su sombrero ocupa la mitad de la imagen.":"Sunlight forms a series of shadow triangles on the great stone staircase. A guide points to the figure that seems to slither down the side of the building. A visitor tries to photograph it, but finds his hat takes up half the picture.","Un grupo escucha la explicación de una guía mientras los pájaros cantan entre los árboles. Un turista aplaude frente a la estructura y escucha un eco extraño. El detective anota que hasta las paredes parecen tener algo que responder.":"A group listens to a guide's explanation while birds sing in the trees. A tourist claps in front of the structure and hears a strange echo. The detective notes that even the walls seem to have something to say.","El calor levanta el olor de la tierra seca y la vegetación. Una familia comparte agua y pequeños paquetes de galletas bajo la sombra de un árbol. Una niña se abanica con un folleto y propone salir antes de que el sol gane la discusión.":"The heat lifts the smell of dry earth and vegetation. A family shares water and little packs of cookies in the shade of a tree. A girl fans herself with a brochure and suggests leaving before the sun wins the argument.","Chichén Itzá fue una importante ciudad de la civilización maya en la península de Yucatán.":"Chichén Itzá was an important city of the Maya civilization on the Yucatán Peninsula.","Cerca de los equinoccios, la luz y la sombra pueden crear una figura que parece una serpiente descendiendo por la escalinata de El Castillo.":"Around the equinoxes, light and shadow can create a figure that looks like a serpent descending the staircase of El Castillo.","Comí un bocadillo después de caminar.":"I ate a sandwich after walking.","Comí cerca de unos jardines antiguos.":"I ate near some old gardens.","Comí después de ver la Fuente de los Leones.":"I ate after seeing the Fountain of the Lions.","Escuché agua correr en un patio.":"I heard water running in a courtyard.","Oí una fuente entre paredes decoradas.":"I heard a fountain between decorated walls.","Escuché agua junto a doce leones de piedra.":"I heard water next to twelve stone lions.","Vi a una guía explicar unos dibujos.":"I saw a guide explaining some patterns.","Vi a un niño contar animales de piedra.":"I saw a boy counting stone animals.","Vi a una guía explicar los palacios nazaríes.":"I saw a guide explaining the Nasrid palaces.","Llevaba un plano de patios y jardines.":"I had a map of courtyards and gardens.","Llevaba una foto del Patio de los Leones.":"I had a photo of the Court of the Lions.","Me fui porque me dolían los pies.":"I left because my feet hurt.","Me fui después de visitar varios patios.":"I left after visiting several courtyards.","Me fui después de contar los doce leones.":"I left after counting the twelve lions.","Estaba en un edificio antiguo.":"I was in an old building.","Estaba en un patio con una fuente.":"I was in a courtyard with a fountain.","Estaba en el Patio de los Leones.":"I was in the Court of the Lions.","Estaba haciendo una visita guiada.":"I was on a guided tour.","Estaba mirando dibujos geométricos en la pared.":"I was looking at geometric patterns on the wall.","Estaba contando los leones de la fuente.":"I was counting the lions on the fountain.","Los patios de la Alhambra en Granada":"The courtyards of the Alhambra in Granada","Un visitante observa los delicados diseños geométricos de una pared mientras una guía explica cómo se repiten las figuras. En el centro del patio, una fuente sostenida por leones de piedra atrae todas las cámaras. El detective sospecha que los animales llevan siglos posando sin cobrar.":"A visitor studies the delicate geometric designs on a wall while a guide explains how the shapes repeat. In the middle of the courtyard, a fountain held up by stone lions attracts every camera. The detective suspects the animals have been posing for centuries without getting paid.","El agua corre suavemente por los canales del patio. Un niño intenta contar los leones de la fuente, pero pierde la cuenta cuando otro visitante pasa frente a él. Su madre propone empezar de nuevo. El niño solicita una calculadora.":"Water flows gently through the courtyard's channels. A boy tries to count the lions on the fountain, but loses count when another visitor walks in front of him. His mother suggests starting over. The boy requests a calculator.","El aroma de los jardines y las plantas cercanas se mezcla con el aire fresco de la mañana. Una viajera guarda una bolsa con un bocadillo y una botella de agua. Después de caminar por varios patios, decide buscar una banca antes de continuar.":"The scent of the gardens and nearby plants mixes with the cool morning air. A traveler packs away a sandwich and a bottle of water. After walking through several courtyards, she decides to find a bench before continuing.","La Alhambra fue ampliada principalmente durante el gobierno de la dinastía nazarí en los siglos XIII y XIV.":"The Alhambra was expanded mainly under the Nasrid dynasty in the 13th and 14th centuries.","La famosa Fuente de los Leones está sostenida por doce esculturas de leones.":"The famous Fountain of the Lions rests on twelve lion sculptures.","Comí pan dulce con mi familia.":"I ate sweet bread with my family.","Comí pan de muerto con chocolate caliente.":"I ate pan de muerto with hot chocolate.","Comí pan de muerto junto a las flores naranjas.":"I ate pan de muerto next to the orange flowers.","Escuché una canción familiar.":"I heard a familiar song.","Oí historias sobre personas muy queridas.":"I heard stories about very dear people.","Escuché la canción favorita de mi abuelo.":"I heard my grandfather's favorite song.","Vi a una niña colocar una fotografía.":"I saw a girl placing a photograph.","Vi a una familia preparar una mesa especial.":"I saw a family preparing a special table.","Vi a una niña poner flores de cempasúchil.":"I saw a girl placing marigold flowers.","Llevaba una fotografía antigua.":"I had an old photograph.","Llevaba velas y flores para recordar a alguien.":"I brought candles and flowers to remember someone.","Llevaba una foto para colocar en la ofrenda.":"I had a photo to place on the ofrenda.","Me fui después de estar con mi familia.":"I left after spending time with my family.","Me fui cuando terminamos de decorar la mesa.":"I left when we finished decorating the table.","Me fui después de recordar a mis seres queridos.":"I left after remembering my loved ones.","Estaba en casa con la familia.":"I was at home with my family.","Estaba junto a una mesa llena de velas.":"I was next to a table full of candles.","Estaba frente a la ofrenda, entre cempasúchil.":"I was in front of the ofrenda, among marigolds.","Estaba recordando a alguien querido.":"I was remembering someone I love.","Estaba encendiendo velas con cuidado.":"I was carefully lighting candles.","Estaba poniendo pan de muerto en la ofrenda.":"I was placing pan de muerto on the ofrenda.","Una ofrenda familiar del Día de Muertos":"A family Day of the Dead altar","Una familia coloca fotografías, velas y flores anaranjadas sobre una mesa decorada. Una niña acomoda con cuidado el retrato de su abuelo. El perro se acerca al pan dulce y recibe una mirada que significa claramente que ese alimento no es para él.":"A family arranges photographs, candles and orange flowers on a decorated table. A girl carefully straightens her grandfather's portrait. The dog approaches the sweet bread and gets a look that clearly means that food is not for him.","Una canción favorita del abuelo suena desde una pequeña bocina mientras la familia comparte recuerdos. Un tío cuenta una historia divertida y todos sonríen. El detective comprende que algunas personas siguen presentes en las conversaciones de quienes las aman.":"Grandpa's favorite song plays from a small speaker while the family shares memories. An uncle tells a funny story and everyone smiles. The detective understands that some people stay present in the conversations of those who love them.","El aroma del copal y las flores se mezcla con el chocolate caliente y el pan recién colocado. Una madre lleva una taza a la mesa, pero el perro vuelve a acercarse. La familia decide mover el plato antes de que el visitante de cuatro patas cometa un robo.":"The aroma of copal and flowers mixes with hot chocolate and freshly placed bread. A mother carries a cup to the table, but the dog comes back. The family decides to move the plate before the four-legged visitor commits a robbery.","El Día de Muertos se celebra principalmente el 1 y 2 de noviembre en México.":"Day of the Dead is celebrated mainly on November 1 and 2 in Mexico.","Las ofrendas pueden incluir fotografías, velas, flores y alimentos que les gustaban a las personas recordadas.":"Ofrendas (home altars) can include photographs, candles, flowers and foods the remembered loved ones enjoyed.","Comí un bocadillo durante el descanso.":"I ate a sandwich during a break.","Comí tortilla de patatas en un pueblo.":"I ate a Spanish omelette in a village.","Comí después de seguir las flechas amarillas.":"I ate after following the yellow arrows.","Escuché campanas desde una iglesia.":"I heard bells from a church.","Oí bastones golpear el camino de piedra.":"I heard walking sticks tapping on the stone path.","Escuché campanas al acercarme a la catedral.":"I heard bells as I approached the cathedral.","Vi a una viajera con una mochila enorme.":"I saw a traveler with a huge backpack.","Vi a un caminante curarse una ampolla.":"I saw a walker treating a blister.","Vi a un peregrino seguir flechas amarillas.":"I saw a pilgrim following yellow arrows.","Llevaba una mochila y una botella.":"I had a backpack and a bottle.","Llevaba un bastón y un mapa de la ruta.":"I had a walking stick and a map of the route.","Llevaba una credencial llena de sellos.":"I had a pilgrim passport full of stamps.","Me fui porque tenía los pies cansados.":"I left because my feet were tired.","Me fui después de descansar en un albergue.":"I left after resting at a hostel.","Me fui cuando mis ampollas pidieron descanso.":"I left when my blisters demanded a break.","Estaba en un camino rural.":"I was on a country road.","Estaba en un albergue lleno de botas.":"I was in a hostel full of boots.","Estaba junto a un mojón con una concha amarilla.":"I was next to a marker with a yellow shell.","Estaba caminando mucho.":"I was walking a lot.","Estaba curándome una ampolla en el talón.":"I was treating a blister on my heel.","Estaba sellando mi credencial de peregrino.":"I was getting my pilgrim passport stamped.","El Camino de Santiago al llegar a Galicia":"The Camino de Santiago arriving in Galicia","Una peregrina camina con una mochila grande y un bastón de madera. Sus botas están cubiertas de polvo y tiene una ampolla en el talón. Cuando ve una señal amarilla que indica la ruta, sonríe como si acabara de encontrar un tesoro.":"A pilgrim walks with a big backpack and a wooden walking stick. Her boots are covered in dust and she has a blister on her heel. When she sees a yellow sign marking the route, she smiles as if she just found treasure.","Las botas golpean el sendero mientras una campana suena desde una iglesia cercana. Un caminante pregunta cuánto falta para llegar al próximo pueblo. Su compañero responde que poco, pero el detective sospecha que sus definiciones de distancia son diferentes.":"Boots thump on the trail while a bell rings from a nearby church. A walker asks how far it is to the next village. His companion says not far, but the detective suspects their definitions of distance are different.","El aroma del pan recién hecho llega desde una cafetería. Dos viajeros comparten una tortilla de patatas y llenan sus botellas de agua. Una peregrina decide quedarse un rato más porque sus pies han presentado una protesta formal.":"The aroma of fresh bread comes from a café. Two travelers share a Spanish omelette and refill their water bottles. A pilgrim decides to stay a little longer because her feet have filed a formal complaint.","El Camino de Santiago es una red de rutas de peregrinación que llevan a Santiago de Compostela.":"The Camino de Santiago is a network of pilgrimage routes that lead to Santiago de Compostela.","La tradición de peregrinar a Santiago de Compostela tiene más de mil años de historia.":"The tradition of walking to Santiago de Compostela is more than a thousand years old.","Comí pescado después de caminar.":"I ate fish after a walk.","Comí un curanto preparado con piedras calientes.":"I ate curanto cooked with hot stones.","Comí curanto después de ver figuras gigantes.":"I ate curanto after seeing giant figures.","Escuché olas y viento cerca de la costa.":"I heard waves and wind near the coast.","Oí el viento pasar entre figuras de piedra.":"I heard the wind blowing between stone figures.","Escuché olas junto a las figuras de Ahu Tongariki.":"I heard waves next to the figures of Ahu Tongariki.","Vi a una guía explicar una tradición.":"I saw a guide explaining a tradition.","Vi a un visitante mirar enormes rostros de piedra.":"I saw a visitor looking at huge stone faces.","Vi a una guía explicar los quince moáis.":"I saw a guide explaining the fifteen moai.","Llevaba agua y una cámara.":"I had water and a camera.","Llevaba un sombrero contra el viento del Pacífico.":"I wore a hat against the Pacific wind.","Llevaba una foto de quince figuras sobre un ahu.":"I had a photo of fifteen figures on an ahu.","Me fui porque el viento era muy fuerte.":"I left because the wind was very strong.","Me fui después de ver las figuras al amanecer.":"I left after seeing the figures at sunrise.","Me fui cuando el sol iluminó los quince moáis.":"I left when the sun lit up the fifteen moai.","Estaba en una isla lejana.":"I was on a remote island.","Estaba en una colina con mucho pasto.":"I was on a grassy hill.","Estaba frente a una fila de moái.":"I was in front of a row of moai.","Estaba haciendo turismo.":"I was sightseeing.","Estaba esquivando caballos salvajes.":"I was dodging wild horses.","Estaba imitando la cara seria de un moái.":"I was copying a moai's serious face.","Los moái de Rapa Nui (Isla de Pascua)":"The moai of Rapa Nui (Easter Island)","Una fila de enormes figuras de piedra mira hacia el interior de la isla, de espaldas al mar. Un turista intenta copiar su expresión seria para una foto, pero se ríe a los tres segundos. El detective concluye que las figuras llevan siglos de práctica.":"A row of enormous stone figures faces inland, with their backs to the sea. A tourist tries to copy their serious expression for a photo, but laughs after three seconds. The detective concludes the figures have had centuries of practice.","El viento del Pacífico silba sobre la hierba mientras unos caballos sueltos pasan cerca del camino. Una guía rapanui explica que está prohibido tocar las figuras o subirse a las plataformas. Un niño baja la mano justo a tiempo.":"The Pacific wind whistles over the grass while loose horses pass near the road. A Rapanui guide explains that touching the figures or climbing the platforms is forbidden. A boy lowers his hand just in time.","Huele a mar, a hierba mojada y a las empanadas de atún que una familia trajo para el almuerzo. Una viajera mira la hora y propone volver al hotel, pero cambia de idea cuando el cielo empieza a ponerse naranja detrás de los gigantes de piedra.":"It smells of the sea, wet grass and the tuna empanadas a family brought for lunch. A traveler checks the time and suggests going back to the hotel, but changes her mind when the sky starts turning orange behind the stone giants.","Rapa Nui está en el océano Pacífico, a más de 3.500 kilómetros de la costa de Chile continental.":"Rapa Nui sits in the Pacific Ocean, more than 3,500 kilometers from mainland Chile.","En la isla hay casi mil moái, tallados en su mayoría en la roca volcánica de la cantera de Rano Raraku.":"The island has almost a thousand moai, most of them carved from the volcanic rock of the Rano Raraku quarry.","Comí algo típico y estaba muy rico.":"I ate something typical and it was delicious.","Probé una comida que no conocía.":"I tried a food I didn't know.","Compré algo para comer mientras caminaba.":"I bought something to eat while I walked.","Comí tanto que olvidé dónde estaba.":"I ate so much I forgot where I was.","Escuché música y muchas conversaciones.":"I heard music and lots of conversations.","Oí a alguien llamar a otra persona.":"I heard someone calling someone else.","Escuché un ruido que me sorprendió.":"I heard a noise that surprised me.","Oí mi estómago pedir otra comida.":"I heard my stomach ask for more food.","Vi a una familia tomando fotografías.":"I saw a family taking photographs.","Hablé con una persona muy amable.":"I talked with a very friendly person.","Vi a alguien trabajando cerca de mí.":"I saw someone working near me.","Vi a un turista más perdido que yo.":"I saw a tourist more lost than me.","Tenía mi teléfono y una mochila.":"I had my phone and a backpack.","Llevaba una bolsa con mis compras.":"I had a bag with my shopping.","Llevaba un mapa, pero estaba al revés.":"I had a map, but it was upside down.","Me fui porque estaba cansado.":"I left because I was tired.","Salí cuando empezó a cambiar el tiempo.":"I left when the weather started to change.","Me fui para conocer otro lugar.":"I left to see another place.","Me fui porque mis pies presentaron una queja.":"I left because my feet filed a complaint.","Estaba en el centro.":"I was downtown.","Estaba en una plaza.":"I was in a square.","Estaba cerca de una iglesia.":"I was near a church.","Estaba en una calle con mucha gente.":"I was on a street full of people.","Estaba paseando.":"I was walking around.","Estaba buscando un baño. Urgente.":"I was looking for a bathroom. Urgently.","Estaba comiendo algo rico.":"I was eating something delicious.","Comí algo que prepararon con cariño.":"I ate something made with love.","Probé un plato que me gustó mucho.":"I tried a dish I really liked.","Compartí comida con otras personas.":"I shared food with other people.","Comí dos veces y dije que era la primera.":"I ate twice and said it was my first time.","Escuché muchas voces conocidas.":"I heard lots of familiar voices.","Oí a alguien dar instrucciones.":"I heard someone giving instructions.","Escuché risas cerca de mí.":"I heard laughter near me.","Escuché mi nombre y fingí no oírlo.":"I heard my name and pretended not to hear it.","Vi a personas que conocía.":"I saw people I knew.","Hablé con alguien de mi familia.":"I talked with someone from my family.","Vi a una persona muy ocupada.":"I saw a very busy person.","Vi a alguien que parecía tener hambre.":"I saw someone who looked hungry.","Llevaba algo para compartir.":"I brought something to share.","Tenía mi teléfono en el bolsillo.":"I had my phone in my pocket.","Llevaba una bolsa pequeña.":"I had a small bag.","Llevaba un regalo y olvidé dónde lo puse.":"I brought a gift and forgot where I put it.","Me fui porque ya era tarde.":"I left because it was late.","Salí después de hablar con todos.":"I left after talking to everyone.","Me fui cuando terminó la actividad.":"I left when the activity ended.","Me fui antes de que me pidieran limpiar.":"I left before they asked me to clean up.","Estaba con la familia.":"I was with the family.","Estaba cerca de la comida.":"I was near the food.","Estaba en una mesa, conversando.":"I was at a table, chatting.","Estaba en un rincón, observando.":"I was in a corner, watching.","Estaba celebrando.":"I was celebrating.","Estaba ayudando un poco.":"I was helping a little.","Estaba comiendo más de la cuenta.":"I was eating more than I should.","Estaba saludando a todo el mundo.":"I was saying hello to everyone.","Comí algo que llevaba en mi mochila.":"I ate something I had in my backpack.","Compartí fruta durante un descanso.":"I shared fruit during a break.","Tomé agua y comí algo sencillo.":"I drank water and ate something simple.","Comí tan rápido que olvidé el sabor.":"I ate so fast I forgot the taste.","Escuché el viento a mi alrededor.":"I heard the wind all around me.","Oí animales a lo lejos.":"I heard animals in the distance.","Escuché un sonido muy fuerte.":"I heard a very loud sound.","Escuché mi barriga pedir comida.":"I heard my belly asking for food.","Vi a una guía explicar el paisaje.":"I saw a guide explaining the landscape.","Vi a turistas tomando fotografías.":"I saw tourists taking photographs.","Hablé con alguien del grupo.":"I talked with someone from the group.","Vi a un turista discutir con su sombrero.":"I saw a tourist arguing with his hat.","Llevaba una mochila con agua.":"I had a backpack with water.","Tenía mi cámara y zapatos cómodos.":"I had my camera and comfortable shoes.","Llevaba ropa para protegerme del clima.":"I wore clothes to protect me from the weather.","Llevaba un mapa que nunca entendí.":"I had a map I never understood.","Regresé cuando cambió el tiempo.":"I went back when the weather changed.","Me fui antes de que oscureciera.":"I left before it got dark.","Me fui porque mis zapatos querían vacaciones.":"I left because my shoes wanted a vacation.","Estaba cerca de un mirador.":"I was near a lookout point.","Estaba lejos de la ciudad.":"I was far from the city.","Estaba disfrutando del paisaje.":"I was enjoying the scenery.","Estaba caminando con cuidado.":"I was walking carefully.","Estaba buscando señal en el teléfono.":"I was looking for phone signal.","Comí algo tradicional de la región.":"I ate something traditional from the region.","Probé una comida después de la visita.":"I tried some food after the visit.","Compartí un bocadillo durante el descanso.":"I shared a sandwich during the break.","Comí tanto que olvidé la explicación.":"I ate so much I forgot the explanation.","Escuché a una guía contar una historia.":"I heard a guide telling a story.","Oí pasos mientras caminábamos.":"I heard footsteps as we walked.","Escuché voces cerca de mí.":"I heard voices near me.","Escuché mi estómago durante la explicación.":"I heard my stomach during the explanation.","Hablé con una guía muy amable.":"I talked with a very friendly guide.","Vi a alguien observar los detalles.":"I saw someone studying the details.","Vi a un turista perder a su grupo.":"I saw a tourist lose his group.","Tenía un folleto de la visita.":"I had a brochure from the visit.","Llevaba una cámara y una mochila.":"I had a camera and a backpack.","Llevaba un mapa que nunca abrí.":"I had a map I never opened.","Me fui después de terminar la visita.":"I left after the visit ended.","Salí porque necesitaba descansar.":"I left because I needed to rest.","Me fui cuando el grupo siguió caminando.":"I left when the group kept walking.","Me fui porque mis pies ya sabían suficiente.":"I left because my feet already knew enough.","Estaba en un lugar histórico.":"I was at a historic place.","Estaba cerca de un guía.":"I was near a guide.","Estaba rodeado de piedras muy antiguas.":"I was surrounded by very old stones.","Estaba con un grupo de turistas.":"I was with a group of tourists.","Estaba aprendiendo algo.":"I was learning something.","Estaba escuchando una explicación.":"I was listening to an explanation.","Estaba tomando fotos de todo.":"I was taking photos of everything.","Estaba fingiendo que entendía todo.":"I was pretending I understood everything.","Un lugar donde las calles cuentan historias y siempre hay algo que descubrir":"A place where the streets tell stories and there's always something to discover","Un momento de la vida cotidiana con familia, amigos o vecinos":"An everyday moment with family, friends or neighbors","Un lugar donde la naturaleza sorprende a quienes se atreven a explorar":"A place where nature surprises those who dare to explore","Un lugar donde el pasado y las tradiciones siguen presentes":"A place where the past and traditions are still alive"}}